<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="EZK" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Ezekiel</para>
  <para style="mt">Ezekiel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now it came to pass in the thirtieth year, in the fourth <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the fifth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, as I <char style="add">[was]</char> among the captives by the river of, <char style="add">[that]</char> the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />In the fifth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, which <char style="add">[was]</char> the fifth year of king Y’hoyakhin’s <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char>’s captivity,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came expressly unto Yechezk’el <char style="add">[God strengthens]</char> the priest, the son of Buzi <char style="add">[my contempt]</char>, in the land of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char> by the river K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>; and the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was there upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And I looked, and, behold, a whirlwind came out of the north, a great cloud, and a fire infolding itself, and a brightness <char style="add">[was]</char> about it, and out of the midst thereof as the colour of amber, out of the midst of the fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Also out of the midst thereof <char style="add">[came]</char> the likeness of four living creatures. And this <char style="add">[was]</char> their appearance; they had the likeness of a man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And everyone had four faces, and everyone had four wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And their feet <char style="add">[were]</char> straight feet; and the sole of their feet <char style="add">[was]</char> like the sole of a calf’s foot: and they sparkled like the colour of burnished brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And <char style="add">[they had]</char> the hands of a man under their wings on their four sides; and they four had their faces and their wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Their wings <char style="add">[were]</char> joined one to another; they turned not when they went; they went everyone straight forward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />As for the likeness of their faces, they four had the face of a man, and the face of a lion, on the right side: and they four had the face of an ox on the left side; they four also had the face of an eagle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus <char style="add">[were]</char> their faces: and their wings <char style="add">[were]</char> stretched upward; two <char style="add">[wings]</char> of everyone <char style="add">[were]</char> joined one to another, and two covered their bodies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they went everyone straight forward: to which the spirit was to go, they went; <char style="add">[and]</char> they turned not when they went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />As for the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance <char style="add">[was]</char> like burning coals of fire, <char style="add">[and]</char> like the appearance of lamps: it went up and down among the living creatures; and the fire was bright, and out of the fire went forth lightning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the living creatures ran and returned as the appearance of a flash of lightning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now as I beheld the living creatures, behold one wheel upon the earth by the living creatures, with his four faces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The appearance of the wheels and their work <char style="add">[was]</char> like unto the colour of a beryl: and they four had one likeness: and their appearance and their work <char style="add">[was]</char> as it were a wheel in the middle of a wheel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />When they went, they went upon their four sides: <char style="add">[and]</char> they turned not when they went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />As for their rings, they were so high that they were dreadful; and their rings <char style="add">[were]</char> full of eyes round about them four.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And when the living creatures went, the wheels went by them: and when the living creatures were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Whithersoever the spirit was to go, they went, there <char style="add">[was their]</char> spirit to go; and the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature <char style="add">[was]</char> in the wheels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />When those went, <char style="add">[these]</char> went; and when those stood, <char style="add">[these]</char> stood; and when those were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature <char style="add">[was]</char> in the wheels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the likeness of the Firmament <char style="pn">(expanse or vault over the earth)</char> upon the heads of the living creature <char style="add">[was]</char> as the colour of the terrible crystal, stretched forth over their heads above.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And under the Firmament <char style="pn">(expanse or vault over the earth)</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> their wings straight, the one toward the other: everyone had two, which covered on this side, and everyone had two, which covered on that side, their bodies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when they went, I heard the noise of their wings, like the noise of great waters, as the voice of the Almighty, the voice of speech, as the noise of an host: when they stood, they let down their wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And there was a voice from the Firmament <char style="pn">(expanse or vault over the earth)</char> that <char style="add">[was]</char> over their heads, when they stood, <char style="add">[and]</char> had let down their wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And above the Firmament <char style="pn">(expanse or vault over the earth)</char> that <char style="add">[was]</char> over their heads <char style="add">[was]</char> the likeness of a throne, as the appearance of a sapphire stone: and upon the likeness of the throne <char style="add">[was]</char> the likeness as the appearance of a man above upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And I saw as the colour of amber, as the appearance of fire round about within it, from the appearance of his waist even upward, and from the appearance of his waist even downward, I saw as it were the appearance of fire, and it had brightness round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />As the appearance of the bow that is in the cloud in the day of rain, so <char style="add">[was]</char> the appearance of the brightness round about. This <char style="add">[was]</char> the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And when I saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, I fell upon my face, and I heard a voice of one that spoke.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, stand upon your<char style="ord">i</char> feet, and I will speak unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the Spirit entered into me when he spoke unto me, and set me upon my feet, that I heard him that spoke unto me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, I send you<char style="ord">i</char> to the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to a rebellious nation that has rebelled against me: they and their fathers have transgressed against me, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto this very day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For <char style="add">[they are]</char> impudent <char style="pn">(shameless; without modesty)</char> children and stiffhearted. I do send you<char style="ord">i</char> unto them; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they, whether they will hear, or whether they will refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>, (for they <char style="add">[are]</char> a rebellious house,) yet shall know that there has been a prophet among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char>, Son of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns <char style="add">[be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> do dwell among scorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they <char style="add">[be]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak my words unto them, whether they will hear, or whether they will refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>: for they <char style="add">[are]</char> most rebellious.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">i</char>, Son of man, hear what I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; Be not you<char style="ord">i</char> rebellious like that rebellious house: open your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and eat that I give you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when I looked, behold, an hand <char style="add">[was]</char> sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book <char style="add">[was]</char> in it;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he spread it before me; and it <char style="add">[was]</char> written within and without: and <char style="add">[there was]</char> written in it lamentations, and mourning, and woe.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that you<char style="ord">i</char> find; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat that roll.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, cause you<char style="ord">i</char> belly to eat, and fill your<char style="ord">i</char> bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> with this roll that I give you<char style="ord">i</char>. Then did I eat <char style="add">[it]</char>; and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, go, get you<char style="ord">i</char> unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and speak with my words unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language, <char style="add">[but]</char> to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Not to many people of a strange speech and of an hard language, whose words you<char style="ord">i</char> can not understand. Surely, had I sent you<char style="ord">i</char> to them, they would have listened unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> will not hearken unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; for they will not hearken unto me: for all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [are]</char> impudent <char style="pn">(shameless; without modesty)</char> and hardhearted.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Behold, I have made your<char style="ord">i</char> face strong against their faces, and your<char style="ord">i</char> forehead strong against their foreheads.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />As an adamant harder than flint have I made your<char style="ord">i</char> forehead: fear them not, neither be dismayed at their looks, though they <char style="add">[be]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, all my words that I shall speak unto you<char style="ord">i</char> receive in your<char style="ord">i</char> heart, and hear with your<char style="ord">i</char> ears.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And go, get you<char style="ord">i</char> to them of the captivity, unto the children of your<char style="ord">i</char> people, and speak unto them, and tell them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; whether they will hear, or whether they will refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then the spirit took me up, and I heard behind me a voice of a great rushing, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> from his place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[I heard]</char> also the noise of the wings of the living creatures that touched one another, and the noise of the wheels over against them, and a noise of a great rushing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So the Spirit lifted me up, and took me away, and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit; but the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was strong upon me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then I came to them of the captivity at Tel-Aviv <char style="add">[mound of the flood]</char>, that dwelt by the river of K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>, and I sat where they sat, and remained there astonished among them seven days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of seven days, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Son of man, I have made you<char style="ord">i</char> a watchman unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: therefore hear the word at my mouth, and give them warning from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />When I say unto the wicked, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die; and you<char style="ord">i</char> give him not warning, nor speak to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life; the same wicked <char style="add">[man]</char> shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet if you<char style="ord">i</char> warn the wicked, and he turn not from his wickedness, nor from his wicked way, he shall die in his iniquity; but you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered your<char style="ord">i</char> soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Again, When a righteous <char style="add">[man]</char> does turn from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, and I lay a stumblingblock before him, he shall die: because you<char style="ord">i</char> have not given him warning, he shall die in his sin, and his righteousness which he has done shall not be remembered; but his blood will I require at your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Nevertheless if you<char style="ord">i</char> warn the righteous <char style="add">[man]</char>, that the righteous sin not, and he does not sin, he shall surely live, because he is warned; also you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered your<char style="ord">i</char> soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was there upon me; and he said unto me, Arise, go forth into the plain, and I will there talk with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then I arose, and went forth into the plain: and, behold, the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stood there, as the glory which I saw by the river of K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>: and I fell on my face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then the Spirit entered into me, and set me upon my feet, and spoke with me, and said unto me, Go, shut yourself within you<char style="ord">i</char> house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Son of man, behold, they shall put bands upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and shall bind you<char style="ord">i</char> with them, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not go out among them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And I will make your<char style="ord">i</char> tongue cleave <char style="pn">(split open; cut open; divide)</char> to the roof of your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be dumb, and shall not be to them a reprover: for they <char style="add">[are]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But when I speak with you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will open your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; He that hears, let him hear; and he that forbears, let him refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>: for they <char style="add">[are]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> also, Son of man, take you<char style="ord">i</char> a tile, and lay it before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and portray upon it the city, <char style="add">[even]</char> Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And lay siege against it, and build a fort against it, and cast a mount against it; set the camp also against it, and set <char style="add">[battering]</char> rams against it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Moreover take you<char style="ord">i</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char> an iron pan, and set it <char style="add">[for]</char> a wall of iron between you<char style="ord">i</char> and the city: and set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against it, and it shall be besieged, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall lay siege against it. This <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a sign to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Lie you<char style="ord">i</char> also upon your<char style="ord">i</char> left side, and lay the iniquity of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> upon it: <char style="add">[according]</char> to the number of the days that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall lie upon it you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bear their iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For I have laid upon you<char style="ord">i</char> the years of their iniquity, according to the number of the days, three hundred and ninety days: so shall you<char style="ord">i</char> bear the iniquity of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">i</char> have accomplished them, lie again on your<char style="ord">i</char> right side, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bear the iniquity of the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> forty days: I have appointed you<char style="ord">i</char> each day for a year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall set your<char style="ord">i</char> face toward the siege of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> arm <char style="add">[shall be]</char> uncovered, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall prophesy against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And, behold, I will lay bands upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not turn you<char style="ord">i</char> from one side to another, till you<char style="ord">i</char> have ended the days of your<char style="ord">i</char> siege.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Take you<char style="ord">i</char> also unto you<char style="ord">i</char> wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentiles, and millet, and fitches <char style="pn">(a kind of grain used for seasoning)</char>, and put them in one vessel, and make you<char style="ord">i</char> bread thereof, <char style="add">[according]</char> to the number of the days that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall lie upon you<char style="ord">i</char> side, three hundred and ninety days shall you<char style="ord">i</char> eat thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> meat which you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat <char style="add">[shall be]</char> by weight, twenty shekels a day: from time to time shall you<char style="ord">i</char> eat it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> shall drink also water by measure, the sixth part of an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char>: from time to time shall you<char style="ord">i</char> drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat it <char style="add">[as]</char> barley cakes, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall bake it with dung that comes out of man, in their sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Even thus shall the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> eat their defiled bread among the Gentiles, to which I will drive them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said I, Ah Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>! behold, my soul has not been polluted: for from my youth up even till now have I not eaten of that which dies of itself, or is torn in pieces; neither came there abominable flesh into my mouth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then he said unto me, Lo, I have given you<char style="ord">i</char> cow’s dung for man’s dung, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall prepare your<char style="ord">i</char> bread with that.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, behold, I will break the staff of bread in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and they shall eat bread by weight, and with care; and they shall drink water by measure, and with astonishment:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />That they may lack bread and water, and be astonished one with another, and consume away for their iniquity.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char>, Son of man, take you<char style="ord">i</char> a sharp knife, take you<char style="ord">i</char> a barber’s razor, and cause <char style="add">[it]</char> to pass upon your<char style="ord">i</char> head and upon your<char style="ord">i</char> beard: then take you<char style="ord">i</char> balances to weigh, and divide the <char style="add">[hair]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> shall burn with fire a third part in the midst of the city, when the days of the siege are fulfilled: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take a third part, <char style="add">[and]</char> strike about it with a knife: and a third part you<char style="ord">i</char> shall scatter in the wind; and I will draw out a sword after them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> shall also take thereof a few in number, and bind them in your<char style="ord">i</char> skirts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then take of them again, and cast them into the midst of the fire, and burn them in the fire; <char style="add">[for]</char> thereof shall a fire come forth into all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; This <char style="add">[is]</char> Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: I have set it in the midst of the nations and countries <char style="add">[that are]</char> round about her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And she has changed my judgments into wickedness more than the nations, and my statutes more than the countries that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about her: for they have refused my judgments and my statutes, they have not walked in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">2f</char> multiplied more than the nations that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about you, <char style="add">[and]</char> have not walked in my statutes, neither have kept my judgments, neither have done according to the judgments of the nations that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about you;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I, even I, <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will execute judgments in the midst of your<char style="ord">i</char> in the sight of the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I will do in you<char style="ord">i</char> that which I have not done, and whereunto I will not do any more the like, because of all you<char style="ord">i</char> abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore the fathers shall eat the sons in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>, and the sons shall eat their fathers; and I will execute judgments in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and the whole remnant of you<char style="ord">i</char> will I scatter into all the winds.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For what reason, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Surely, because you<char style="ord">i</char> have defiled my sanctuary with all your<char style="ord">i</char> detestable things, and with all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations, therefore will I also diminish <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>; neither shall my eye spare, neither will I have any pity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />A third part of you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die with the pestilence, and with famine shall they be consumed in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>: and a third part shall fall by the sword round about you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I will scatter a third part into all the winds, and I will draw out a sword after them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus shall my anger be accomplished, and I will cause my fury to rest upon them, and I will be comforted: and they shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char> in my zeal, when I have accomplished my fury in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Moreover I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> waste, and a reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> among the nations that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about you<char style="ord">i</char>, in the sight of all that pass by.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So it shall be a reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> and a taunt, an instruction and an astonishment unto the nations that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about you<char style="ord">i</char>, when I shall execute judgments in you<char style="ord">i</char> in anger and in fury and in furious rebukes. I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />When I shall send upon them the evil arrows of famine, which shall be for <char style="add">[their]</char> destruction, <char style="add">[and]</char> which I will send to destroy you: and I will increase the famine upon you, and will break your staff of bread:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />So will I send upon you famine and evil beasts, and they shall bereave you<char style="ord">i</char>; and pestilence and blood shall pass through you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I will bring the sword upon you<char style="ord">i</char>. I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face toward the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and prophesy against them,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say, You<char style="ord">2f</char> mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, hear the word of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys; Behold, I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I, will bring a sword upon you, and I will destroy your high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And your altars shall be desolate, and your images shall be broken: and I will cast down your slain <char style="add">[men]</char> before your idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I will lay the dead carcasses of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> before their idols; and I will scatter your bones round about your altars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In all your dwelling places the cities shall be laid waste, and the high places shall be desolate; that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your images may be cut down, and your works may be abolished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the slain shall fall in the midst of you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Yet will I leave a remnant, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may have <char style="add">[some]</char> that shall escape the sword among the nations, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be scattered through the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they that escape of you shall remember me among the nations to which they shall be carried captives, because I am broken with their whorish heart, which has departed from me, and with their eyes, which go a whoring after their idols: and they shall loathe themselves for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[and that]</char> I have not said in vain that I would do this evil unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Strike with your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and stamp with your<char style="ord">i</char> foot, and say, Alas for all the evil abominations of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>! for they shall fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />He that is far off shall die of the pestilence; and he that is near shall fall by the sword; and he that remains and is besieged shall die by the famine: thus will I accomplish my fury upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when their slain <char style="add">[men]</char> shall be among their idols round about their altars, upon every high hill, in all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak, the place where they did offer soothing aroma to all their idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So will I stretch out my hand upon them, and make the land desolate, yes, more desolate than the wilderness toward Divlah <char style="add">[the place of the fig cake]</char>, in all their habitations: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Also, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> unto the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; An end, the end is come upon the four corners of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now <char style="add">[is]</char> the end <char style="add">[come]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will send my anger upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will judge you<char style="ord">i</char> according to your<char style="ord">i</char> ways, and will recompense upon you<char style="ord">i</char> all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And my eye shall not spare you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither will I have pity: but I will recompense your<char style="ord">i</char> ways upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations shall be in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; An evil, an only evil, behold, is come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />An end is come, the end is come: it watch for you<char style="ord">i</char>; behold, it is come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The morning is come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, O you<char style="ord">i</char> that dwell in the land: the time is come, the day of trouble <char style="add">[is]</char> near, and not the sounding again of the mountains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now will I shortly pour out my fury upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and accomplish my anger upon you<char style="ord">i</char>: and I will judge you<char style="ord">i</char> according to your<char style="ord">i</char> ways, and will recompense you<char style="ord">i</char> for all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And my eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: I will recompense you<char style="ord">i</char> according to your<char style="ord">i</char> ways and your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations <char style="add">[that]</char> are in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> Yehovah Makeh <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate Striking {You}]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Behold the day, behold, it is come: the morning is gone forth; the rod has blossomed, pride has budded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Violence is risen up into a rod of wickedness: none of them <char style="add">[shall remain]</char>, nor of their multitude, nor of any of theirs: neither <char style="add">[shall there be]</char> wailing for them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The time is come, the day draws near: let not the buyer rejoice, nor the seller mourn: for wrath <char style="add">[is]</char> upon all the multitude thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For the seller shall not return to that which is sold, although they were yet alive: for the vision <char style="add">[is]</char> touching the whole multitude thereof, <char style="add">[which]</char> shall not return; neither shall any strengthen himself in the iniquity of his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />They have blown the trumpet, even to make all ready; but none goes to the battle: for my wrath <char style="add">[is]</char> upon all the multitude thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The sword <char style="add">[is]</char> without, and the pestilence and the famine within: he that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the field shall die with the sword; and he that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the city, famine and pestilence shall devour him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But they that escape of them shall escape, and shall be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, all of them mourning, everyone for his iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />All hands shall be feeble, and all knees shall be weak <char style="add">[as]</char> water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />They shall also gird <char style="add">[themselves]</char> with sackcloth, and horror shall cover them; and shame <char style="add">[shall be]</char> upon all faces, and baldness upon all their heads.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />They shall cast their silver in the streets, and their gold shall be removed: their silver and their gold shall not be able to deliver them in the day of the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: they shall not satisfy their souls, neither fill their bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char>: because it is the stumbling block of their iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />As for the beauty of his ornament, he set it in majesty: but they made the images of their abominations <char style="add">[and]</char> of their detestable things in it: therefore have I set it far from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And I will give it into the hands of the strangers for a prey, and to the wicked of the earth for a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>; and they shall pollute it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />My face will I turn also from them, and they shall pollute my secret <char style="add">[place]</char>: for the robbers shall enter into it, and defile it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Make a chain: for the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For what reason I will bring the worst of the heathen, and they shall possess their houses: I will also make the pomp of the strong to cease; and their holy places shall be defiled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Destruction comes; and they shall seek peace, and <char style="add">[there shall be]</char> none.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Mischief shall come upon mischief, and rumour shall be upon rumour; then shall they seek a vision of the prophet; but the law shall perish from the priest, and counsel from the ancients.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />The king shall mourn, and the prince shall be clothed with desolation, and the hands of the people of the land shall be troubled: I will do unto them after their way, and according to their deserts will I judge them; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the sixth year, in the sixth <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the fifth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[as]</char> I sat in my house, and the elders of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sat before me, that the hand of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> fell there upon me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then I beheld, and lo a likeness as the appearance of fire: from the appearance of his waist even downward, fire; and from his waist even upward, as the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he put forth the form of an hand, and took me by a lock of my head; and the Spirit lifted me up between the earth and the heaven, and brought me in the visions of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to the door of the inner gate that looks toward the north; where <char style="add">[was]</char> the seat of the image of jealousy, which provokes to jealousy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And, behold, the glory of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [was]</char> there, according to the vision that I saw in the plain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Son of man, lift up your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes now the way toward the north. So I lifted up my eyes the way toward the north, and behold northward at the gate of the altar this image of jealousy in the entry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />He said furthermore unto me, Son of man, see you<char style="ord">i</char> what they do? <char style="add">[even]</char> the great abominations that the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> commit here, that I should go far off from my sanctuary? but turn you<char style="ord">i</char> yet again, <char style="add">[and]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see greater abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he brought me to the door of the court; and when I looked, behold a hole in the wall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Son of man, dig now in the wall: and when I had excavated in the wall, behold a door.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said unto me, Go in, and behold the wicked abominations that they do here.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So I went in and saw; and behold every form of creeping things, and abominable beasts, and all the idols of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, portrayed upon the wall round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And there stood before them seventy men of the elders of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and in the midst of them stood Ya’azanyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, with every man his censer in his hand; and a thick cloud of incense went up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Son of man, have you<char style="ord">i</char> seen what the ancients of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> do in the dark, every man in the chambers of his imagery? for they say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sees us not; the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has forsaken the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />He said also unto me, Turn you<char style="ord">i</char> yet again, <char style="add">[and]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see greater abominations that they do.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then he brought me to the door of the gate of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house which <char style="add">[was]</char> toward the north; and, behold, there sat women weeping for Tammuz <char style="pn">(a Babylonian goddess)</char> <char style="add">[sprout of life]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> seen <char style="add">[this]</char>, O Son of man? turn you<char style="ord">i</char> yet again, <char style="add">[and]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see greater abominations than these.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he brought me into the inner court of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house, and, behold, at the door of the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, between the porch and the altar, <char style="add">[were]</char> about five and twenty men, with their backs toward the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and their faces toward the east; and they worshipped the sun toward the east.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then he said unto me, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> seen <char style="add">[this]</char>, O Son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> that they commit the abominations which they commit here? for they have filled the land with violence, and have returned to provoke me to anger: and, lo, they put the branch to their nose.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Therefore will I also deal in fury: my eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: and though they cry in my ears with a loud voice, <char style="add">[yet]</char> will I not hear them.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />He cried also in my ears with a loud voice, saying, Cause them that have charge over the city to draw near, even every man <char style="add">[with]</char> his destroying weapon in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And, behold, six men came from the way of the higher gate, which lies toward the north, and every man a slaughter weapon in his hand; and one man among them <char style="add">[was]</char> clothed with linen, with a writer’s inkhorn by his side: and they went in, and stood beside the brazen altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the glory of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> was gone up from the cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, whereupon he was, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man clothed with linen, which <char style="add">[had]</char> the writer’s inkhorn by his side;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And to the others he said in my hearing, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char> after him through the city, and strike: let not your eye spare, neither have you<char style="ord">2f</char> pity:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Slay utterly old <char style="add">[and]</char> young, both maids, and little children, and women: but come not near any man upon whom <char style="add">[is]</char> the mark; and begin at my sanctuary. Then they began at the ancient men which <char style="add">[were]</char> before the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he said unto them, Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain: go you<char style="ord">2f</char> forth. And they went forth, and killed in the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it came to pass, while they were slaying them, and I was left, that I fell upon my face, and cried, and said, Ah Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>! will you<char style="ord">i</char> destroy all the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> pouring out of your<char style="ord">i</char> fury upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then said he unto me, The iniquity of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [is]</char> exceeding great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perverseness: for they say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has forsaken the earth, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sees not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And as for me also, my eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity, <char style="add">[but]</char> I will recompense their way upon their head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And, behold, the man clothed with linen, which <char style="add">[had]</char> the inkhorn by his side, reported the matter, saying, I have done as you<char style="ord">i</char> have commanded me.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then I looked, and, behold, in the Firmament <char style="pn">(expanse or vault over the earth)</char> that was above the head of the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> there appeared over them as it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he spoke unto the man clothed with linen, and said, Go in between the wheels, <char style="add">[even]</char> under the cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, and fill your<char style="ord">i</char> hand with coals of fire from between the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, and scatter <char style="add">[them]</char> over the city. And he went in in my sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> stood on the right side of the house, when the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went up from the cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, <char style="add">[and stood]</char> over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> glory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the sound of the k’vurim (cherubim)’ wings was heard <char style="add">[even]</char> to the outer court, as the voice of the Almighty <char style="pn">(Shaddai)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> when he speaks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> when he had commanded the man clothed with linen, saying, Take fire from between the wheels, from between the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>; then he went in, and stood beside the wheels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> stretched forth his hand from between the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> unto the fire that <char style="add">[was]</char> between the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, and took <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> into the hands of <char style="add">[him that was]</char> clothed with linen: who took <char style="add">[it]</char>, and went out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And there appeared in the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> the form of a man’s hand under their wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when I looked, behold the four wheels by the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, one wheel by one cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, and another wheel by another cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>: and the appearance of the wheels <char style="add">[was]</char> as the colour of a beryl stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> their appearances, they four had one likeness, as if a wheel had been in the midst of a wheel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />When they went, they went upon their four sides; they turned not as they went, but to the place to which the head looked they followed it; they turned not as they went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And their whole body, and their backs, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, <char style="add">[were]</char> full of eyes round about, <char style="add">[even]</char> the wheels that they four had.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />As for the wheels, it was cried unto them in my hearing, O wheel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And everyone had four faces: the first face <char style="add">[was]</char> the face of a cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, and the second face <char style="add">[was]</char> the face of a man, and the third the face of a lion, and the fourth the face of an eagle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> were lifted up. This <char style="add">[is]</char> the living creature that I saw by the river of K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> went, the wheels went by them: and when the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, the same wheels also turned not from beside them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />When they stood, <char style="add">[these]</char> stood; and when they were lifted up, <char style="add">[these]</char> lifted up themselves <char style="add">[also]</char>: for the spirit of the living creature <char style="add">[was]</char> in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> lifted up their wings, and mounted up from the earth in my sight: when they went out, the wheels also <char style="add">[were]</char> beside them, and <char style="add">[everyone]</char> stood at the door of the east gate of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house; and the glory of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [was]</char> over them above.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the living creature that I saw under the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by the river of K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>; and I knew that they <char style="add">[were]</char> the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Every one had four faces apiece, and everyone four wings; and the likeness of the hands of a man <char style="add">[was]</char> under their wings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the likeness of their faces <char style="add">[was]</char> the same faces which I saw by the river of K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>, their appearances and themselves: they went everyone straight forward.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover the spirit lifted me up, and brought me unto the east gate of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house, which looks eastward: and behold at the door of the gate five and twenty men; among whom I saw Ya’azanyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the son of ‘Azur <char style="add">[he that assists]</char>, and P’latyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah delivers]</char> the son of B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char>, princes of the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Son of man, these <char style="add">[are]</char> the men that devise mischief, and give wicked counsel in this city:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Which say, <char style="add">[It is]</char> not near; let us build houses: this <char style="add">[city is]</char> the caldron, and we <char style="add">[be]</char> the flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Therefore prophesy against them, prophesy, O Son of man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fell upon me, and said unto me, Speak; Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Thus have you<char style="ord">2f</char> said, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for I know the things that come into your mind, <char style="add">[everyone of]</char> them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have multiplied your slain in this city, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> have filled the streets thereof with the slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Your slain whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> have laid in the midst of it, they <char style="add">[are]</char> the flesh, and this <char style="add">[city is]</char> the caldron: but I will bring you forth out of the midst of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have feared the sword; and I will bring a sword upon you, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I will bring you out of the midst thereof, and deliver you into the hands of strangers, and will execute judgments among you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall fall by the sword; I will judge you in the border of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />This <char style="add">[city]</char> shall not be your caldron, neither shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> be the flesh in the midst thereof; <char style="add">[but]</char> I will judge you in the border of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not walked in my statutes, neither executed my judgments, but have done after the manners of the heathen that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it came to pass, when I prophesied, that P’latyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah delivers]</char> the son of B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> died. Then fell I down upon my face, and cried with a loud voice, and said, Ah Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>! will you<char style="ord">i</char> make a full end of the remnant of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Son of man, you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren, the men of your<char style="ord">i</char> family, and all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> wholly, <char style="add">[are]</char> they unto whom the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> have said, Get you far from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: unto us is this land given in possession.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Therefore say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Although I have cast them far off among the heathen, and although I have scattered them among the countries, yet will I be to them as a little sanctuary in the countries where they shall come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Therefore say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will even gather you from the people, and assemble you out of the countries where you<char style="ord">2f</char> have been scattered, and I will give you the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they shall come there, and they shall take away all the detestable things thereof and all the abominations thereof from there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And I will give them one heart, and I will put a new spirit within you; and I will take the stony heart out of their flesh, and will give them an heart of flesh:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />That they may walk in my statutes, and keep my ordinances, and do them: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But <char style="add">[as for them]</char> whose heart walks after the heart of their detestable things and their abominations, I will recompense their way upon their own heads, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then did the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> lift up their wings, and the wheels beside them; and the glory of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [was]</char> over them above.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> went up from the midst of the city, and stood upon the mountain which <char style="add">[is]</char> on the east side of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Afterwards the spirit took me up, and brought me in a vision by the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> into Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>, to them of the captivity. So the vision that I had seen went up from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then I spoke unto them of the captivity all the things that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had showed me.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> also came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, you<char style="ord">i</char> dwell in the midst of a rebellious house, which have eyes to see, and see not; they have ears to hear, and hear not: for they <char style="add">[are]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Therefore, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, prepare your<char style="ord">i</char> stuff for removing, and remove by day in their sight; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall remove from your<char style="ord">i</char> place to another place in their sight: it may be they will consider, though they <char style="add">[be]</char> a rebellious house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">i</char> bring forth your<char style="ord">i</char> stuff by day in their sight, as stuff for removing: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go forth at even in their sight, as they that go forth into captivity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Dig you<char style="ord">i</char> through the wall in their sight, and carry out thereby.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In their sight shall you<char style="ord">i</char> bear <char style="add">[it]</char> upon <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> shoulders, <char style="add">[and]</char> carry <char style="add">[it]</char> forth in the twilight: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall cover your<char style="ord">i</char> face, that you<char style="ord">i</char> see not the ground: for I have set you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[for]</char> a sign unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I did so as I was commanded: I brought forth my stuff by day, as stuff for captivity, and in the even I excavated through the wall with my hand; I brought <char style="add">[it]</char> forth in the twilight, <char style="add">[and]</char> I bore <char style="add">[it]</char> upon <char style="add">[my]</char> shoulder in their sight.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And in the morning came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Son of man, has not the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the rebellious house, said unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, What do you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Say you<char style="ord">i</char> unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; This burden <char style="add">[concern]</char> the prince in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that <char style="add">[are]</char> among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Say, I <char style="add">[am]</char> your sign: like as I have done, so shall it be done unto them: they shall remove <char style="add">[and]</char> go into captivity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the prince that <char style="add">[is]</char> among them shall bear upon <char style="add">[his]</char> shoulder in the twilight, and shall go forth: they shall dig through the wall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> carry out thereby: he shall cover his face, that he see not the ground with <char style="add">[his]</char> eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />My net also will I spread upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare: and I will bring him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion] [to]</char> the land of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>; yet shall he not see it, though he shall die there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will scatter toward every wind all that <char style="add">[are]</char> about him to help him, and all his bands; and I will draw out the sword after them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I shall scatter them among the nations, and disperse them in the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But I will leave a few men of them from the sword, from the famine, and from the pestilence; that they may declare all their abominations among the heathen to which they come; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Son of man, eat your<char style="ord">i</char> bread with quaking, and drink your<char style="ord">i</char> water with trembling and with carefulness;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And say unto the people of the land, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> of the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> of the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; They shall eat their bread with carefulness, and drink their water with astonishment, that her land may be desolate from all that is in it, because of the violence of all them that dwell in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the cities that are inhabited shall be laid waste, and the land shall be desolate; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Son of man, what <char style="add">[is]</char> that proverb <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> have in the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, The days are prolonged, and every vision fails?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Tell them therefore, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will make this proverb to cease, and they shall no more use it as a proverb in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; but say unto them, The days are at hand, and the effect of every vision.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For there shall be no more any vain vision nor flattering divination within the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />For I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: I will speak, and the word that I shall speak shall come to pass; it shall be no more prolonged: for in your days, O rebellious house, will I say the word, and will perform it, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Son of man, behold, <char style="add">[they of]</char> the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> say, The vision that he sees <char style="add">[is]</char> for many days <char style="add">[to come]</char>, and he prophesies of the times <char style="add">[that are]</char> far off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Therefore say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; There shall none of my words be prolonged any more, but the word which I have spoken shall be done, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that prophesy, and say you<char style="ord">i</char> unto them that prophesy out of their own hearts, Hear you<char style="ord">2f</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Woe unto the foolish prophets, that follow their own spirit, and have seen nothing!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, your<char style="ord">i</char> prophets are like the foxes in the deserts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> have not gone up into the gaps, neither made up the hedge for the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to stand in the battle in the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />They have seen vanity and lying divination, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> says: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not sent them: and they have made <char style="add">[others]</char> to hope that they would confirm the word.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not seen a vain vision, and have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not spoken a lying divination, whereas you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> says <char style="add">[it]</char>; albeit <char style="pn">(although it be that)</char> I have not spoken?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have spoken vanity, and seen lies, therefore, behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And my hand shall be upon the prophets that see vanity, and that divine lies: they shall not be in the assembly of my people, neither shall they be written in the writing of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, neither shall they enter into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Because, even because they have seduced my people, saying, Peace; and <char style="add">[there was]</char> no peace; and one built up a wall, and, lo, others daubed it with untempered <char style="add">[mortar]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Say unto them which daub <char style="pn">(to cover or plaster)</char> <char style="add">[it]</char> with untempered <char style="add">[mortar]</char>, that it shall fall: there shall be an overflowing shower; and you<char style="ord">2f</char>, O great hailstones, shall fall; and a stormy wind shall rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Lo, when the wall is fallen, shall it not be said unto you, Where <char style="add">[is]</char> the daubing which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have daubed <char style="add">[it]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will even rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> <char style="add">[it]</char> with a stormy wind in my fury; and there shall be an overflowing shower in my anger, and great hailstones in <char style="add">[my]</char> fury to consume <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So will I break down the wall that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have daubed with untempered <char style="add">[mortar]</char>, and bring it down to the ground, so that the foundation thereof shall be discovered, and it shall fall, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be consumed in the midst thereof: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Thus will I accomplish my wrath upon the wall, and upon them that have daubed it with untempered <char style="add">[mortar]</char>, and will say unto you, The wall <char style="add">[is]</char> no <char style="add">[more]</char>, neither they that daubed it;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[To wit]</char>, the prophets of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> which prophesy concerning Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and which see visions of peace for her, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> no peace, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Likewise, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against the daughters of your<char style="ord">i</char> people, which prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy you<char style="ord">i</char> against them,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Woe to the <char style="add">[women]</char> that sew pillows to all armholes, and make kerchiefs upon the head of every stature to hunt souls! Will you<char style="ord">2f</char> hunt the souls of my people, and will you<char style="ord">2f</char> save the souls alive <char style="add">[that come]</char> unto you?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And will you<char style="ord">2f</char> pollute me among my people for handfuls of barley and for pieces of bread, to slay the souls that should not die, and to save the souls alive that should not live, by your lying to my people that hear <char style="add">[your]</char> lies?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />For what reason thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against your pillows, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> there hunt the souls to make <char style="add">[them]</char> fly, and I will tear them from your arms, and will let the souls go, <char style="add">[even]</char> the souls that you<char style="ord">2f</char> hunt to make <char style="add">[them]</char> fly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Your kerchiefs also will I tear, and deliver my people out of your hand, and they shall be no more in your hand to be hunted; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Because with lies you<char style="ord">2f</char> have made the heart of the righteous sad, whom I have not made sad; and strengthened the hands of the wicked, that he should not return from his wicked way, by promising him life:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Therefore you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall see no more vanity, nor divine divinations: for I will deliver my people out of your hand: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then came certain of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto me, and sat before me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Son of man, these men have set up their idols in their heart, and put the stumbling block of their iniquity before their face: should I be enquired of at all by them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Therefore speak unto them, and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Every man of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that sets up his idols in his heart, and puts the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and comes to the prophet; I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will answer him that comes according to the multitude of his idols;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />That I may take the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in their own heart, because they are all estranged from me through their idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Therefore say unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Repent, and turn <char style="add">[yourselves]</char> from your idols; and turn away your faces from all your abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For every one of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, or of the stranger that sojourns in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which separates himself from me, and sets up his idols in his heart, and puts the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and comes to a prophet to enquire of him concerning me; I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will answer him by myself:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will set my face against that man, and will make him a sign and a proverb, and I will cut him off from the midst of my people; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And if the prophet be deceived when he has spoken a thing, I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have deceived that prophet, and I will stretch out my hand upon him, and will destroy him from the midst of my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they shall bear the punishment of their iniquity: the punishment of the prophet shall be even as the punishment of him that seeks <char style="add">[unto him]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />That the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> may go no more astray from me, neither be polluted any more with all their transgressions; but that they may be my people, and I may be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again to me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Son of man, when the land sins against me by trespassing grievously, then will I stretch out my hand upon it, and will break the staff of the bread thereof, and will send famine upon it, and will cut off man and beast from it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Though these three men, Noach <char style="add">[rest]</char>, Dani’el <char style="add">[God is Judge]</char>, and Job, were in it, they should deliver <char style="add">[but]</char> their own souls by their righteousness, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />If I cause destructive <char style="pn">(hurtful; noxious)</char> beasts to pass through the land, and they spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> it, so that it be desolate, that no man may pass through because of the beasts:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Though]</char> these three men <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters; they only shall be delivered, but the land shall be desolate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Or <char style="add">[if]</char> I bring a sword upon that land, and say, Sword, go through the land; so that I cut off man and beast from it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Though these three men <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters, but they only shall be delivered themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Or <char style="add">[if]</char> I send a pestilence into that land, and pour out my fury upon it in blood, to cut off from it man and beast:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Though No’ah <char style="add">[Motion]</char>, Dani’el <char style="add">[God is Judge]</char>, and Job, <char style="add">[were]</char> in it, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, they shall deliver neither son nor daughter; they shall <char style="add">[but]</char> deliver their own souls by their righteousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; How much more when I send my four sore judgments upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, the sword, and the famine, and the destructive <char style="pn">(hurtful; noxious)</char> beast, and the pestilence, to cut off from it man and beast?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Yet, behold, in it shall be left a remnant that shall be brought forth, <char style="add">[both]</char> sons and daughters: behold, they shall come forth unto you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall see their way and their doings: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be comforted concerning the evil that I have brought upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> concerning all that I have brought upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they shall comfort you, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> see their ways and their doings: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I have not done without cause all that I have done in it, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, What is the vine tree more than any tree, <char style="add">[or than]</char> a branch which is among the trees of the forest?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Shall wood be taken thereof to do any work? or will <char style="add">[men]</char> take a pin of it to hang any vessel thereon?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Behold, it is cast into the fire for fuel; the fire devours both the ends of it, and the midst of it is burned. Is it meet for <char style="add">[any]</char> work?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Behold, when it was whole, it was meet for no work: how much less shall it be meet yet for <char style="add">[any]</char> work, when the fire has devoured it, and it is burned?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; As the vine tree among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so will I give the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will set my face against them; they shall go out from <char style="add">[one]</char> fire, and <char style="add">[another]</char> fire shall devour them; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I set my face against them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will make the land desolate, because they have committed a trespass, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, cause Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to know her abominations,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; You<char style="ord">1s</char> birth and you<char style="ord">i</char> nativity <char style="add">[is]</char> of the land of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> father <char style="add">[was]</char> an Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> mother an Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> nativity, in the day you<char style="ord">i</char> were born your<char style="ord">i</char> navel was not cut, neither were you<char style="ord">i</char> washed in water to supple <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> were not salted at all, nor swaddled at all.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />None eye pitied you<char style="ord">i</char>, to do any of these unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to have compassion upon you<char style="ord">i</char>; but you<char style="ord">i</char> were cast out in the open field, to the loathing of you<char style="ord">i</char> person, in the day that you<char style="ord">i</char> were born.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when I passed by you<char style="ord">i</char>, and saw you<char style="ord">i</char> polluted in your<char style="ord">i</char> own blood, I said unto you<char style="ord">i</char> [when you<char style="ord">i</char> were] in your<char style="ord">i</char> blood, Live; yes, I said unto you<char style="ord">i</char> [when you<char style="ord">i</char> were] in your<char style="ord">i</char> blood, Live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />I have caused you<char style="ord">i</char> to multiply as the bud of the field, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have increased and waxen great, and you<char style="ord">i</char> are come to excellent ornaments: <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> breasts are fashioned, and your<char style="ord">i</char> hair is grown, whereas you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> naked and bare.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now when I passed by you<char style="ord">i</char>, and looked upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> time <char style="add">[was]</char> the time of love; and I spread my skirt over you<char style="ord">i</char>, and covered your<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness: yes, I swore unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and entered into a covenant with you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> became mine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then washed I you<char style="ord">i</char> with water; yes, I thoroughly washed away your<char style="ord">i</char> blood from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I anointed you<char style="ord">i</char> with oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />I clothed you<char style="ord">i</char> also with adorned with needlework work, and shod you<char style="ord">i</char> with badgers’ skin, and I girded you<char style="ord">i</char> about with fine linen, and I covered you<char style="ord">i</char> with silk.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />I decked you<char style="ord">i</char> also with ornaments, and I put bracelets upon your<char style="ord">i</char> hands, and a chain on your<char style="ord">i</char> neck.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I put a jewel on your<char style="ord">i</char> forehead, and earrings in your<char style="ord">i</char> ears, and a beautiful crown upon your<char style="ord">i</char> head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus were you<char style="ord">i</char> decked with gold and silver; and your<char style="ord">i</char> clothing <char style="add">[was of]</char> fine linen, and silk, and adorned with needlework work; you<char style="ord">i</char> did eat fine flour, and honey, and oil: and you<char style="ord">i</char> were exceeding beautiful, and you<char style="ord">i</char> did prosper into a kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And your<char style="ord">i</char> renown <char style="pn">(great reputation; being well-known)</char> went forth among the heathen for your<char style="ord">i</char> beauty: for it <char style="add">[was]</char> perfect through my comeliness, which I had put upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">i</char> did trust in your<char style="ord">i</char> own beauty, and played the prostitute because of your<char style="ord">i</char> renown (great reputation; being well-known), and poured out your<char style="ord">i</char> fornications on everyone that passed by; his it was.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And of your<char style="ord">i</char> garments you<char style="ord">i</char> did take, and decked you<char style="ord">i</char> high places with diverse colours, and played the prostitute thereupon: <char style="add">[the like things]</char> shall not come, neither shall it be <char style="add">[so]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have also taken your<char style="ord">i</char> fair jewels of my gold and of my silver, which I had given you<char style="ord">i</char>, and made to yourself images of men, and did commit whoredom with them,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And took your<char style="ord">i</char> embroidered garments, and covered them: and you<char style="ord">i</char> have set my oil and my incense before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />My meat also which I gave you<char style="ord">i</char>, fine flour, and oil, and honey, <char style="add">[which]</char> I fed you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> have even set it before them for a soothing aroma: and <char style="add">[thus]</char> it was, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> have taken your<char style="ord">i</char> sons and your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have borne unto me, and these have you<char style="ord">i</char> sacrificed unto them to be devoured. <char style="add">[Is this]</char> of your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution a small matter,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />That you<char style="ord">i</char> have slain my children, and delivered them to cause them to pass through <char style="add">[the fire]</char> for them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And in all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations and your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution you<char style="ord">i</char> have not remembered the days of your<char style="ord">i</char> youth, when you<char style="ord">i</char> were naked and bare, <char style="add">[and]</char> were polluted in your<char style="ord">i</char> blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass after all your<char style="ord">i</char> wickedness, (woe, woe unto you<char style="ord">i</char>! says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have also built unto you<char style="ord">i</char> an eminent place, and have made you<char style="ord">i</char> an high place in every street.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have built your<char style="ord">i</char> high place at every head of the way, and have made your<char style="ord">i</char> beauty to be abhorred, and have opened your<char style="ord">i</char> legs to everyone that passed by, and multiplied your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have also committed fornication with the Mitzri your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbours, great of flesh; and have increased your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution, to provoke me to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Behold, therefore I have stretched out my hand over you<char style="ord">i</char>, and have diminished your<char style="ord">i</char> ordinary <char style="add">[food]</char>, and delivered you<char style="ord">i</char> unto the will of them that hate you<char style="ord">i</char>, the daughters of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, which are ashamed of your<char style="ord">i</char> lewd way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have played the whore also with the children of Ashur, because you<char style="ord">i</char> were insatiable; yes, you<char style="ord">i</char> have played the prostitute with them, and yet could not be satisfied.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have moreover multiplied your<char style="ord">i</char> fornication in the land of Kena’an <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> unto Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>; and yet you<char style="ord">i</char> were not satisfied with this!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />How weak is your<char style="ord">i</char> heart, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, seeing you<char style="ord">i</char> do all these <char style="add">[things]</char>, the work of an shameless whorish woman;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />In that you<char style="ord">i</char> build your<char style="ord">i</char> eminent place in the head of every way, and makes your<char style="ord">i</char> high place in every street; and have not been as an prostitute, in that you<char style="ord">i</char> scorn getting paid;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[But as]</char> a wife that commits adultery, <char style="add">[which]</char> takes strangers instead of her husband!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />They give gifts to all whores: but you<char style="ord">i</char> give your<char style="ord">i</char> gifts to all your<char style="ord">i</char> lovers, and hire them, that they may come unto you<char style="ord">i</char> on every side for your<char style="ord">i</char> whoredom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the contrary is in you<char style="ord">i</char> from <char style="add">[other]</char> women in your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution, whereas none follows you<char style="ord">i</char> to commit cult prostitution: and in that you<char style="ord">i</char> give a reward, and no reward is given unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> are contrary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />For this reason, O prostitute, hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> filthiness was poured out, and your<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness discovered through your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution with your<char style="ord">i</char> lovers, and with all the idols of your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations, and by the blood of your<char style="ord">i</char> children, which you<char style="ord">i</char> did give unto them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Behold, therefore I will gather all your<char style="ord">i</char> lovers, with whom you<char style="ord">i</char> have taken pleasure, and all <char style="add">[them]</char> that you<char style="ord">i</char> have loved, with all <char style="add">[them]</char> that you<char style="ord">i</char> have hated; I will even gather them roundabout against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will expose your<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness unto them, that they may see all your<char style="ord">i</char> nakedness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And I will judge you<char style="ord">i</char>, as women that breaks wedlock and sheds blood are judged; and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> blood in fury and jealousy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And I will also give you<char style="ord">i</char> into their hand, and they shall throw down your<char style="ord">i</char> eminent place, and shall break down your<char style="ord">i</char> high places: they shall strip you<char style="ord">i</char> also of your<char style="ord">i</char> clothes, and shall take your<char style="ord">i</char> fair jewels, and leave your<char style="ord">i</char> naked and bare.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />They shall also bring up a company against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and they shall stone you<char style="ord">i</char> with stones, and thrust you<char style="ord">i</char> through with their swords.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And they shall burn your<char style="ord">i</char> houses with fire, and execute judgments upon you<char style="ord">i</char> in the sight of many women: and I will cause you<char style="ord">i</char> to cease from playing the prostitute, and you<char style="ord">i</char> also shall give no pay <char style="pn">(to your lovers)</char> any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />So will I make my fury toward you<char style="ord">i</char> to rest, and my jealousy shall depart from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will be quiet, and will be no more angry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have not remembered the days of your<char style="ord">i</char> youth, but have fretted me in all these <char style="add">[things]</char>; behold, therefore I also will recompense your<char style="ord">i</char> way upon <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> head, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not commit this lewdness above all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />Behold, everyone that uses proverbs shall use <char style="add">[this]</char> proverb against you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, As <char style="add">[is]</char> the mother, <char style="add">[so is]</char> her daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> mother’s daughter, that loathes her husband and her children; and you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the sister of your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters, which loathed their husbands and their children: your mother <char style="add">[was]</char> an Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and your father an Emori <char style="add">[Rebellious Highlanders]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And your<char style="ord">i</char> elder sister <char style="add">[is]</char> Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, she and her daughters that dwell at your<char style="ord">i</char> left hand: and your<char style="ord">i</char> younger sister, that dwells at your<char style="ord">i</char> right hand, <char style="add">[is]</char> S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> and her daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />Yet have you<char style="ord">i</char> not walked after their ways, nor done after their abominations: but, as <char style="add">[if that were]</char> a very little <char style="add">[thing]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> were corrupted more than they in all your<char style="ord">i</char> ways!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> sister has not done, she nor her daughters, as you<char style="ord">i</char> have done, you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />Behold, this was the iniquity of your<char style="ord">i</char> sister S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char>, pride, fullness of bread, and abundance of idleness was in her and in her daughters, neither did she strengthen the hand of the poor and needy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And they were arrogant <char style="pn">(proud; lifted up)</char>, and committed abomination before me: therefore I took them away as I saw <char style="add">[good]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />Neither has Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> committed half of your<char style="ord">i</char> sins; but you<char style="ord">i</char> have multiplied your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations more than they, and have justified your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters in all your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations which you<char style="ord">i</char> have done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> also, which have judged your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters, bear your<char style="ord">i</char> own shame for your<char style="ord">i</char> sins that you<char style="ord">i</char> have committed more abominable than they: they are more righteous than you<char style="ord">i</char>: yes, be you<char style="ord">i</char> confounded also, and bear your<char style="ord">i</char> shame, in that you<char style="ord">i</char> have justified your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />When I shall bring again their captivity, the captivity of S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> and her daughters, and the captivity of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> and her daughters, then <char style="add">[will I bring again]</char> the captivity of your<char style="ord">i</char> captives in the midst of them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" />That you<char style="ord">i</char> may bear your<char style="ord">i</char> own shame, and may be confounded in all that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done, in that you<char style="ord">i</char> are a comfort unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" />When your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters, S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> and her daughters, shall return to their former estate, and Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> and her daughters shall return to their former estate, then you<char style="ord">i</char> and your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters shall return to your former estate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" />For your<char style="ord">i</char> sister S’dom <char style="add">[Burning]</char> was not mentioned by your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth in the day of your<char style="ord">i</char> pride,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" />Before your<char style="ord">i</char> wickedness was discovered, as at the time of <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> of the daughters of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and all <char style="add">[that are]</char> round about her, the daughters of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, which despise you<char style="ord">i</char> round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have borne your<char style="ord">i</char> lewdness and your<char style="ord">i</char> abominations, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will even deal with you<char style="ord">i</char> as you<char style="ord">i</char> have done, which have despised the oath in breaking the Covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="60" style="v" />Nevertheless I will remember my covenant with you<char style="ord">i</char> in the days of your<char style="ord">i</char> youth, and I will establish unto you<char style="ord">i</char> an everlasting covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="61" style="v" />Then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall remember your<char style="ord">i</char> ways, and be ashamed, when you<char style="ord">i</char> shall receive your<char style="ord">i</char> sisters, your<char style="ord">i</char> elder and your<char style="ord">i</char> younger: and I will give them unto you<char style="ord">i</char> for daughters, but not by your<char style="ord">i</char> covenant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="62" style="v" />And I will establish my covenant with you<char style="ord">i</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="63" style="v" />That you<char style="ord">i</char> may remember, and be confounded, and never open your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth anymore because of your<char style="ord">i</char> shame, when I am pacified toward you<char style="ord">i</char> for all that you<char style="ord">i</char> have done, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, put forth a riddle, and speak a parable unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; A great eagle with great wings, longwinged, full of feathers, which had diverse colours, came unto L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and took the highest branch of the cedar:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />He cropped off the top of his young twigs, and carried it into a land of traffick <char style="pn">(trade; do business)</char>; he set it in a city of merchants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He took also of the seed of the land, and planted it in a fruitful field; he placed <char style="add">[it]</char> by great waters, <char style="add">[and]</char> set it <char style="add">[as]</char> a willow tree.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it grew, and became a spreading vine of low stature, whose branches turned toward him, and the roots thereof were under him: so it became a vine, and brought forth branches, and shot forth sprigs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />There was also another great eagle with great wings and many feathers: and, behold, this vine did bend her roots toward him, and shot forth her branches toward him, that he might water it by the furrows of her plantation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />It was planted in a good soil by great waters, that it might bring forth branches, and that it might bear fruit, that it might be a goodly vine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Say you<char style="ord">i</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Shall it prosper? shall he not pull up the roots thereof, and cut off the fruit thereof, that it wither? it shall wither in all the leaves of her spring, even without great power or many people to pluck it up by the roots thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Yes, behold, <char style="add">[being]</char> planted, shall it prosper? shall it not utterly wither, when the east wind touches it? it shall wither in the furrows where it grew.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Say now to the rebellious house, Know you<char style="ord">2f</char> not what these <char style="add">[things mean]</char>? tell <char style="add">[them]</char>, Behold, the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> is come to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and has taken the king thereof, and the princes thereof, and led them with him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And has taken of the king’s seed, and made a covenant with him, and has taken an oath of him: he has also taken the mighty of the land:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />That the kingdom might be base, that it might not lift itself up, <char style="add">[but]</char> that by keeping of his covenant it might stand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But he rebelled against him in sending his ambassadors into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, that they might give him horses and much people. Shall he prosper? shall he escape that does such <char style="add">[things]</char>? or shall he break the covenant, and be delivered?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, surely in the place <char style="add">[where]</char> the king <char style="add">[dwells]</char> that made him king, whose oath he despised, and whose covenant he broke, <char style="add">[even]</char> with him in the midst of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> he shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Neither shall Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> with <char style="add">[his]</char> mighty army and great company make for him in the war, by casting up mounts, and building forts, to cut off many persons:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Seeing he despised the oath by breaking the covenant, when, lo, he had given his hand, and has done all these <char style="add">[things]</char>, he shall not escape.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, surely my oath that he has despised, and my covenant that he has broken, even it will I recompense upon his own head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And I will spread my net upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare, and I will bring him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and will plead with him there for his trespass that he has trespassed against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And all his fugitives with all his bands shall fall by the sword, and they that remain shall be scattered toward all winds: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will also take of the highest branch of the high cedar, and will set <char style="add">[it]</char>; I will crop off from the top of his young twigs a tender one, and will plant <char style="add">[it]</char> upon an high mountain and eminent:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In the mountain of the height of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> will I plant it: and it shall bring forth boughs, and bear fruit, and be a goodly cedar: and under it shall dwell all fowl of every wing; in the shadow of the branches thereof shall they dwell.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And all the trees of the field shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have brought down the high tree, have exalted the low tree, have dried up the green tree, and have made the dry tree to flourish: I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken and have done <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me again, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />What mean you<char style="ord">2f</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> use this proverb concerning the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the children’s teeth are set on edge?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not have <char style="add">[occasion]</char> any more to use this proverb in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Behold, all souls are my; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son is my: the soul that sins, it shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> has not eaten upon the mountains, neither has lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, neither has defiled his neighbour’s wife, neither has come near to a monstrous woman,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And has not oppressed any, <char style="add">[but]</char> has restored to the debtor his pledge, has spoiled none by violence, has given his bread to the hungry, and has covered the naked with a garment;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He <char style="add">[that]</char> has not given forth upon usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char>, neither has taken any increase, <char style="add">[that]</char> has withdrawn his hand from iniquity, has executed true judgment between man and man,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Has walked in my statutes, and has kept my judgments, to deal truly; he <char style="add">[is]</char> just, he shall surely live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />If he beget <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> a son <char style="add">[that is]</char> a robber, a shedder of blood, and <char style="add">[that]</char> does the like to <char style="add">[any]</char> one of these <char style="add">[things]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And that does not any of those <char style="add">[duties]</char>, but even has eaten upon the mountains, and defiled his neighbour’s wife,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Has oppressed the poor and needy, has spoiled by violence, has not restored the pledge, and has lifted up his eyes to the idols, has committed abomination,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Has given forth upon usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char>, and has taken increase: shall he then live? he shall not live: he has done all these abominations; he shall surely die; his blood shall be upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now, lo, <char style="add">[if]</char> he beget <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> a son, that sees all his father’s sins which he has done, and considers, and does not such like,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> has not eaten upon the mountains, neither has lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, has not defiled his neighbour’s wife,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Neither has oppressed any, has not withheld the pledge, neither has spoiled by violence, <char style="add">[but]</char> has given his bread to the hungry, and has covered the naked with a garment,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> has taken off his hand from the poor, <char style="add">[that]</char> has not received usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char> nor increase, has executed my judgments, has walked in my statutes; he shall not die for the iniquity of his father, he shall surely live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As for]</char> his father, because he cruelly oppressed, spoiled his brother by violence, and did <char style="add">[that]</char> which <char style="add">[is]</char> not good among his people, lo, even he shall die in his iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet say you<char style="ord">2f</char>, Why? does not the son bear the iniquity of the father? When the son has done that which is lawful and right, <char style="add">[and]</char> has kept all my statutes, and has done them, he shall surely live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />The soul that sins, it shall die. The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, neither shall the father bear the iniquity of the son: the righteousness of the righteous shall be upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked shall be upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But if the wicked will turn from all his sins that he has committed, and keep all my statutes, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall surely live, he shall not die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />All his transgressions that he has committed, they shall not be mentioned unto him: in his righteousness that he has done he shall live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Have I any pleasure at all that the wicked should die? says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: <char style="add">[and]</char> not that he should return from his ways, and live?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />But when the righteous turns away from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, <char style="add">[and]</char> does according to all the abominations that the wicked <char style="add">[man]</char> does, shall he live? All his righteousness that he has done shall not be mentioned: in his trespass that he has trespassed, and in his sin that he has sinned, in them shall he die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, The way of the Lord is not equal. Hear now, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; Is not my way equal? are not your ways unequal?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />When a righteous <char style="add">[man]</char> turns away from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, and dies in them; for his iniquity that he has done shall he die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Again, when the wicked <char style="add">[man]</char> turns away from his wickedness that he has committed, and does that which is lawful and right, he shall save his soul alive.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Because he considers, and turns away from all his transgressions that he has committed, he shall surely live, he shall not die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Yet says the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, The way of the Lord is not equal. O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, are not my ways equal? are not your ways unequal?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Therefore I will judge you, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, everyone according to his ways, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>. Repent, and turn <char style="add">[yourselves]</char> from all your transgressions; so iniquity shall not be your ruin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Cast away from you all your transgressions, whereby you<char style="ord">2f</char> have transgressed; and make you a new heart and a new spirit: for why will you<char style="ord">2f</char> die, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />For I have no pleasure in the death of him that dies, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: wherefore turn <char style="add">[yourselves]</char>, and live you<char style="ord">2f</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover take you<char style="ord">i</char> up a lamentation for the princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And say, What <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> mother? A lioness: she lay down among lions, she nourished her whelps among young lions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And she brought up one of her whelps: it became a young lion, and it learned to catch the prey; it devoured men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The nations also heard of him; he was taken in their pit, and they brought him with chains unto the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now when she saw that she had waited, <char style="add">[and]</char> her hope was lost, then she took another of her whelps, <char style="add">[and]</char> made him a young lion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he went up and down among the lions, he became a young lion, and learned to catch the prey, <char style="add">[and]</char> devoured men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he knew their desolate palaces, and he laid waste their cities; and the land was desolate, and the fullness thereof, by the noise of his roaring.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then the nations set against him on every side from the provinces, and spread their net over him: he was taken in their pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they put him in ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> in chains, and brought him to the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>: they brought him into holds, that his voice should no more be heard upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> mother <char style="add">[is]</char> like a vine in your<char style="ord">i</char> blood, planted by the waters: she was fruitful and full of branches by reason of many waters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And she had strong rods for the scepters of them that bore rule, and her stature was exalted among the thick branches, and she appeared in her height with the multitude of her branches.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />But she was plucked up in fury, she was cast down to the ground, and the east wind dried up her fruit: her strong rods were broken and withered; the fire consumed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And now she <char style="add">[is]</char> planted in the wilderness, in a dry and thirsty ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And fire is gone out of a rod of her branches, <char style="add">[which]</char> has devoured her fruit, so that she has no strong rod <char style="add">[to be]</char> a scepter to rule. This <char style="add">[is]</char> a lamentation, and shall be for a lamentation.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the seventh year, in the fifth <char style="add">[month]</char>, the tenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> certain of the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came to enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and sat before me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Son of man, speak unto the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Are you<char style="ord">2f</char> come to enquire of me? <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, I will not be enquired of by you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Will you<char style="ord">i</char> judge them, Son of man, will you<char style="ord">i</char> judge <char style="add">[them]</char>? cause them to know the abominations of their fathers:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; In the day when I chose Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and lifted up my hand unto the seed of the house of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and made myself known unto them in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, when I lifted up my hand unto them, saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In the day <char style="add">[that]</char> I lifted up my hand unto them, to bring them forth of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> into a land that I had discovered <char style="pn">(spied out; examined)</char> for them, flowing with milk and honey, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the glory of all lands:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then said I unto them, Cast you<char style="ord">2f</char> away every man the abominations of his eyes, and defile not yourselves with the idols of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But they rebelled against me, and would not hearken unto me: they did not every man cast away the abominations of their eyes, neither did they forsake the idols of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: then I said, I will pour out my fury upon them, to accomplish my anger against them in the midst of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But I wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, among whom they <char style="add">[were]</char>, in whose sight I made myself known unto them, in bringing them forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For what reason I caused them to go forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and brought them into the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I gave them my statutes, and showed them my judgments, which <char style="add">[if]</char> a man do, he shall even live in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Moreover also I gave them my Shabbat, to be a sign between me and them, that they might know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rebelled against me in the wilderness: they walked not in my statutes, and they despised my judgments, which <char style="add">[if]</char> a man do, he shall even live in them; and my Shabbat they greatly polluted: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them in the wilderness, to consume them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But I wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, in whose sight I brought them out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Yet also I lifted up my hand unto them in the wilderness, that I would not bring them into the land which I had given <char style="add">[them]</char>, flowing with milk and honey, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the glory of all lands;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Because they despised my judgments, and walked not in my statutes, but polluted my Shabbat: for their heart went after their idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Nevertheless my eye spared them from destroying them, neither did I make an end of them in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />But I said unto their children in the wilderness, Walk you<char style="ord">2f</char> not in the statutes of your fathers, neither observe their judgments, nor defile yourselves with their idols:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; walk in my statutes, and keep my judgments, and do them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> my Shabbat; and they shall be a sign between me and you, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yet the children rebelled against me: they walked not in my statutes, neither kept my judgments to do them, which <char style="add">[if]</char> a man do, he shall even live in them; they polluted my Shabbat: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them, to accomplish my anger against them in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Nevertheless I withdrew my hand, and wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted in the sight of the heathen, in whose sight I brought them forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />I lifted up my hand unto them also in the wilderness, that I would scatter them among the heathen, and disperse them through the countries;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Because they had not executed my judgments, but had despised my statutes, and had polluted my Shabbat, and their eyes were after their fathers’ idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Wherefore I permitted them, or gave them over to, <char style="add">[false]</char> statutes that are not good, and judgments whereby they should not live.;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And I polluted them in their own gifts, in that they caused to pass through <char style="add">[the fire]</char> all that opens the womb, that I might make them desolate, to the end that they might know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Therefore, Son of man, speak unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Yet in this your fathers have blasphemed me, in that they have committed a trespass against me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[For]</char> when I had brought them into the land, <char style="add">[for]</char> the which I lifted up my hand to give it to them, then they saw every high hill, and all the thick trees, and they offered there their sacrifices, and there they presented the provocation of their offering: there also they made their soothing aroma, and poured out there their drink offerings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then I said unto them, What <char style="add">[is]</char> the high place whereunto you<char style="ord">2f</char> go? And the name thereof is called Bamah <char style="add">[high place]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />For what reason say unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Are you<char style="ord">2f</char> polluted after the manner of your fathers? and commit you<char style="ord">2f</char> whoredom after their abominations?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />For when you<char style="ord">2f</char> offer your gifts, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> make your sons to pass through the fire, you<char style="ord">2f</char> pollute yourselves with all your idols, even unto this day: and shall I be enquired of by you, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, I will not be enquired of by you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And that which comes into your mind shall not be at all, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, We will be as the heathen, as the families of the countries, to serve wood and stone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, surely with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out, will I rule over you:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And I will bring you out from the people, and will gather you out of the countries wherein you<char style="ord">2f</char> are scattered, with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And I will bring you into the wilderness of the people, and there will I plead with you face to face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Like as I pleaded with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, so will I plead with you, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And I will cause you to pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And I will purge out from among you the rebels, and them that transgress against me: I will bring them forth out of the country where they sojourn, and they shall not enter into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />As for you, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, serve you<char style="ord">2f</char> everyone his idols, and hereafter <char style="add">[also]</char>, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> will not hearken unto me: but pollute you<char style="ord">2f</char> my holy name no more with your gifts, and with your idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />For in my holy mountain, in the mountain of the height of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, there shall all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, all of them in the land, serve me: there will I accept them, and there will I require your offerings, and the firstfruits of your oblations, with all your holy things.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />I will accept you with your soothing aroma, when I bring you out from the people, and gather you out of the countries wherein you<char style="ord">2f</char> have been scattered; and I will be sanctified in you before the heathen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I shall bring you into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, into the country <char style="add">[for]</char> the which I lifted up my hand to give it to your fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And there shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> remember your ways, and all your doings, wherein you<char style="ord">2f</char> have been defiled; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall loathe yourselves in your own sight for all your evils that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have committed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have wrought with you for my name’s sake, not according to your wicked ways, nor according to your corrupt doings, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />Son of man, set you<char style="ord">i</char> face toward the south, and drop <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> word]</char> toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the south field;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And say to the forest of the south, Hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will kindle a fire in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and it shall devour every green tree in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and every dry tree: the flaming flame shall not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north shall be burned in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And all flesh shall see that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have kindled it: it shall not be quenched.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />Then said I, Ah Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>! they say of me, Does he not speak parables?</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face toward Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and drop <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> word]</char> toward the holy places, and prophesy against the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say to the and of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will draw forth my sword out of his sheath, and will cut off from you<char style="ord">i</char> the righteous and the wicked.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Seeing then that I will cut off from you<char style="ord">i</char> the righteous and the wicked, therefore shall my sword go forth out of his sheath against all flesh from the south to the north:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />That all flesh may know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have drawn forth my sword out of his sheath: it shall not return any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Sigh therefore, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, with the breaking of <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> waist; and with bitterness sigh before their eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it shall be, when they say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, For what reason sigh you<char style="ord">i</char>? that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall answer, For the tidings; because it comes: and every heart shall melt, and all hands shall be feeble, and every spirit shall faint, and all knees shall be weak <char style="add">[as]</char> water: behold, it comes, and shall be brought to pass, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Son of man, prophesy, and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>; Say, A sword, a sword is sharpened, and also furbished:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />It is sharpened to make a sore slaughter; it is furbished that it may glitter: should we then make gladness? it scorns the rod of my son, <char style="add">[as]</char> every tree.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he has given it to be furbished, that it may be handled: this sword is sharpened, and it is furbished, to give it into the hand of the slayer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Cry and howl, Son of man: for it shall be upon my people, it <char style="add">[shall be]</char> upon all the princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: terrors by reason of the sword shall be upon my people: strike therefore upon <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> thigh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Because <char style="add">[it is]</char> a trial, and what if <char style="add">[the sword]</char> contemn <char style="pn">(despise with mockery; show contempt)</char> even the rod? it shall be no <char style="add">[more]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> therefore, Son of man, prophesy, and strike <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hands together, and let the sword be doubled the third time, the sword of the slain: it <char style="add">[is]</char> the sword of the great <char style="add">[men that are]</char> slain, which enters into their private chambers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />I have set the point of the sword against all their gates, that <char style="add">[their]</char> heart may faint, and <char style="add">[their]</char> ruins be multiplied: ah! <char style="add">[it is]</char> made bright, <char style="add">[it is]</char> wrapped up for the slaughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Go you<char style="ord">i</char> one way or other, <char style="add">[either]</char> on the right hand, <char style="add">[or]</char> on the left, to wherever your<char style="ord">i</char> face <char style="add">[is]</char> set.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />I will also strike my hands together, and I will cause my fury to rest: I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have said <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me again, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Also, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, appoint you<char style="ord">i</char> two ways, that the sword of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> may come: both two shall come forth out of one land: and choose you<char style="ord">i</char> a place, choose <char style="add">[it]</char> at the head of the way to the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Appoint a way, that the sword may come to Rabbah <char style="add">[Great] [Great]</char> of the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> the fortified.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> stood at the parting of the way, at the head of the two ways, to use divination: he made <char style="add">[his]</char> arrows bright, he consulted with images, he looked in the liver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />At his right hand was the divination for Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to appoint captains, to open the mouth in the slaughter, to lift up the voice with shouting, to appoint <char style="add">[battering]</char> rams against the gates, to cast a mount, <char style="add">[and]</char> to build a fort.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it shall be unto them as a false divination in their sight, to them that have sworn oaths: but he will call to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> remembrance the iniquity, that they may be taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have made your iniquity to be remembered, in that your transgressions are discovered, so that in all your doings your sins do appear; because, <char style="add">[I say]</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> are come to remembrance, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be taken with the hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char>, Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> wicked prince of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, whose day is come, when iniquity <char style="add">[shall have]</char> an end,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Remove the Diadem <char style="pn">(royal headband worn by Eastern kings)</char>, and take off the crown: this <char style="add">[shall]</char> not <char style="add">[be]</char> the same: exalt <char style="add">[him that is]</char> low, and abase <char style="add">[him that is]</char> high.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />I will overturn, overturn, overturn, it: and it shall be no <char style="add">[more]</char>, until he come whose right it is; and I will give it <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char>, Son of man, prophesy and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> concerning the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and concerning their reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char>; even say you<char style="ord">i</char>, The sword, the sword <char style="add">[is]</char> drawn: for the slaughter <char style="add">[it is]</char> furbished, to consume because of the glittering:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Whiles they see vanity unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, whiles they divine a lie unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to bring you<char style="ord">i</char> upon the necks of <char style="add">[them that are]</char> slain, of the wicked, whose day is come, when their iniquity <char style="add">[shall have]</char> an end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Shall I cause <char style="add">[it]</char> to return into his sheath? I will judge you<char style="ord">i</char> in the place where you<char style="ord">i</char> were created, in the land of your<char style="ord">i</char> nativity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And I will pour out my indignation upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will blow against you<char style="ord">i</char> in the fire of my wrath, and deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> into the hand of cruel men, <char style="add">[and]</char> skillful to destroy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> shall be for fuel to the fire; your<char style="ord">i</char> blood shall be in the midst of the land; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be no <char style="add">[more]</char> remembered: for I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Now, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, will you<char style="ord">i</char> judge, will you<char style="ord">i</char> judge the bloody city? yes, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall show her all her abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then say you<char style="ord">i</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, The city sheds blood in the midst of it, that her time may come, and makes idols against herself to defile herself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> are become guilty in your<char style="ord">i</char> blood that you<char style="ord">i</char> have shed; and have defiled yourself in your<char style="ord">i</char> idols which you<char style="ord">i</char> have made; and you<char style="ord">i</char> have caused your<char style="ord">i</char> days to draw near, and are come <char style="add">[even]</char> unto your<char style="ord">i</char> years: therefore have I made you<char style="ord">i</char> a reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> unto the heathen, and a mocking to all countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Those that be]</char> near, and <char style="add">[those that be]</char> far from you<char style="ord">i</char>, shall mock you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[which are]</char> infamous <char style="add">[and]</char> much vexed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Behold, the princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, everyone were in you<char style="ord">i</char> to their power to shed blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In you<char style="ord">i</char> have they make light of father and mother: in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> have they dealt by oppression with the stranger: in you<char style="ord">i</char> have they wronged the fatherless and the widow.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have despised my holy things, and have profaned my Shabbat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />In you<char style="ord">i</char> are men that carry tales to shed blood: and in you<char style="ord">i</char> they eat upon the mountains: in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> they commit lewdness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />In you<char style="ord">i</char> have they discovered their fathers’ nakedness: in you<char style="ord">i</char> have they forced her that was set apart for pollution <char style="pn">(her menstrual cycle)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And one has committed abomination with his neighbour’s wife; and another has lewdly defiled his daughter in law; and another in you<char style="ord">i</char> has humbled his sister, his father’s daughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />In you<char style="ord">i</char> have they taken gifts to shed blood; you<char style="ord">i</char> have taken usury <char style="pn">(interest paid for using money)</char> and increase, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have greedily gained of your<char style="ord">i</char> neighbours by extortion, and have forgotten me, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Behold, therefore I have smitten my hand at your<char style="ord">i</char> dishonest gain which you<char style="ord">i</char> have made, and at your<char style="ord">i</char> blood which has been in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Can your<char style="ord">i</char> heart endure, or can your<char style="ord">i</char> hands be strong, in the days that I shall deal with you<char style="ord">i</char>? I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, and will do <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And I will scatter you<char style="ord">i</char> among the heathen, and disperse you<char style="ord">i</char> in the countries, and will consume your<char style="ord">i</char> filthiness out of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take your<char style="ord">i</char> inheritance in yourself in the sight of the heathen, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Son of man, the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> is to me become dross: all they <char style="add">[are]</char> brass, and tin, and iron, and lead, in the midst of the furnace; they are <char style="add">[even]</char> the dross of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">2f</char> are all become dross, behold, therefore I will gather you into the midst of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> they gather silver, and brass, and iron, and lead, and tin, into the midst of the furnace, to blow the fire upon it, to melt <char style="add">[it]</char>; so will I gather <char style="add">[you]</char> in my anger and in my fury, and I will leave <char style="add">[you there]</char>, and melt you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yes, I will gather you, and blow upon you in the fire of my wrath, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be melted in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />As silver is melted in the midst of the furnace, so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> be melted in the midst thereof; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have poured out my fury upon you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Son of man, say unto her, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the land that is not cleansed, nor rained upon in the day of indignation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> a conspiracy of her prophets in the midst thereof, like a roaring lion ravening <char style="pn">(preying upon to devour)</char> the prey; they have devoured souls; they have taken the treasure and precious things; they have made her many widows in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Her priests have violated my law, and have profaned my holy things: they have put no difference between the holy and Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char>, neither have they showed <char style="add">[difference]</char> between the unclean and the clean, and have hid their eyes from my Shabbat, and I am profaned among them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Her princes in the midst thereof <char style="add">[are]</char> like wolves ravening <char style="pn">(preying upon to devour)</char> the prey, to shed blood, <char style="add">[and]</char> to destroy souls, to get dishonest gain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And her prophets have daubed them with untempered <char style="add">[mortar]</char>, seeing vanity, and divining lies unto them, saying, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not spoken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />The people of the land have used oppression, and exercised robbery, and have vexed the poor and needy: yes, they have oppressed the stranger wrongfully.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And I sought for a man among them, that should make up the hedge, and stand in the gap before me for the land, that I should not destroy it: but I found none.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Therefore have I poured out my indignation upon them; I have consumed them with the fire of my wrath: their own way have I recompensed upon their heads, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, there were two women, the daughters of one mother:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they committed cult prostitution in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; they committed cult prostitution in their youth: there were their breasts pressed, and there they bruised the nipples of their virginity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the names of them <char style="add">[were]</char> Oholah <char style="add">[her own tent]</char> the elder, and Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char> her sister: and they were my, and they bore sons and daughters. Thus <char style="add">[were]</char> their names; Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain] [is]</char> Oholah <char style="add">[her own tent]</char>, and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Oholah <char style="add">[her own tent]</char> played the prostitute when she was mine; and she doted on her lovers, on the children of Ashur <char style="add">[her]</char> neighbours,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Which were]</char> clothed with blue, captains and rulers, all of them desirable young men, horsemen riding upon horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus she committed her cult prostitution with them, with all them <char style="add">[that were]</char> the chosen men of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and with all on whom she doted: with all their idols she defiled herself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Neither left she her cult prostitution <char style="add">[brought]</char> from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: for in her youth they lay with her, and they bruised the breasts of her virginity, and poured their lust <char style="pn">(fornication)</char> upon her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For what reason I have delivered her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the children of Ashur, upon whom she doted.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />These discovered her nakedness: they took her sons and her daughters, and killed her with the sword: and she became notorious among women; for they had executed judgment upon her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And when her sister Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char> saw <char style="add">[this]</char>, she was more corrupt in her inordinate <char style="pn">(unrestrained; immoderate)</char> love than she, and in her cult prostitution more than her sister in <char style="add">[her]</char> cult prostitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />She doted upon the children of Ashur <char style="add">[her]</char> neighbours, captains and rulers clothed most gorgeously, horsemen riding upon horses, all of them desirable young men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then I saw that she was defiled, <char style="add">[that]</char> they <char style="add">[took]</char> both one way,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And <char style="add">[that]</char> she increased her cult prostitution: for when she saw men portrayed upon the wall, the images of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char> portrayed with vermilion,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Girded with girdles upon their waist, exceeding in dyed attire upon their heads, all of them princes to look to, after the manner of the Bavlim <char style="add">[confusion (my mixing)]</char> of Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>, the land of their nativity:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And as soon as she saw them with her eyes, she doted upon them, and sent messengers unto them into Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the Bavlim <char style="add">[confusion (my mixing)]</char> came to her into the bed of love, and they defiled her with their lust, and she was polluted with them, and her mind was alienated from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />So she discovered her cult prostitution, and discovered her nakedness: then my mind was alienated from her, like as my mind was alienated from her sister.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet she multiplied her cult prostitution, in calling to remembrance the days of her youth, wherein she had played the prostitute in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />For she doted upon their paramours, whose flesh <char style="add">[is as]</char> the flesh of asses, and whose issue <char style="pn">(what comes forth)</char> <char style="add">[is like]</char> the issue <char style="pn">(what comes forth)</char> of horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Thus you<char style="ord">i</char> longed for the lewdness of your<char style="ord">i</char> youth, in fondling youti nipples by the Mitzri for the breasts of your<char style="ord">i</char> youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Therefore, O Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char>, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will raise up your<char style="ord">i</char> lovers against you<char style="ord">i</char>, from whom your<char style="ord">i</char> mind is alienated, and I will bring them against you<char style="ord">i</char> on every side;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />The children of Bavel (to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity), and all the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers]</char>, P’kod <char style="add">[visitation]</char>, and Shoa <char style="add">[rich]</char>, and Koa <char style="add">[he-camel]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the children of Ashur with them: all of them desirable young men, captains and rulers, great lords and renowned, all of them riding upon horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they shall come against you<char style="ord">i</char> with chariots, wagons, and wheels, and with an assembly of people, <char style="add">[which]</char> shall set against your<char style="ord">i</char> buckler <char style="pn">(round shielf held with a grip)</char> and shield and helmet round about: and I will set judgment before them, and they shall judge you<char style="ord">i</char> according to their judgments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And I will set my jealousy against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and they shall deal furiously with you<char style="ord">i</char>: they shall take away your<char style="ord">i</char> nose and your<char style="ord">i</char> ears; and your<char style="ord">i</char> remnant shall fall by the sword: they shall take your<char style="ord">i</char> sons and your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters; and your<char style="ord">i</char> residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> shall be devoured by the fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />They shall also strip you<char style="ord">i</char> out of your<char style="ord">i</char> clothes, and take away your<char style="ord">i</char> fair jewels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Thus will I make your<char style="ord">i</char> lewdness to cease from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> whoredom <char style="add">[brought]</char> from the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: so that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not lift up your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes unto them, nor remember Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> into the hand <char style="add">[of them]</char> whom you<char style="ord">i</char> hate, into the hand <char style="add">[of them]</char> from whom your<char style="ord">i</char> mind is alienated:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they shall deal with you<char style="ord">i</char> hatefully, and shall take away all your<char style="ord">i</char> labour, and shall leave you<char style="ord">i</char> naked and bare: and the nakedness of your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution shall be discovered, both your<char style="ord">i</char> lewdness and your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />I will do these <char style="add">[things]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, because you<char style="ord">i</char> have gone a whoring after the heathen, <char style="add">[and]</char> because you<char style="ord">i</char> are polluted with their idols.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />You<char style="ord">i</char> have walked in the way of your<char style="ord">i</char> sister; therefore will I give her cup into your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall drink of your<char style="ord">i</char> sister’s cup deep and large: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be laughed to scorn and had in ridicule <char style="pn">(laughing at enemies’ threats)</char>; it contains much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be filled with drunkenness and sorrow, with the cup of astonishment and desolation, with the cup of your<char style="ord">i</char> sister Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall even drink it and suck <char style="add">[it]</char> out, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall break the shards thereof, and pluck off your<char style="ord">i</char> own breasts: for I have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have forgotten me, and cast me behind your<char style="ord">i</char> back, therefore bear you<char style="ord">i</char> also your<char style="ord">i</char> lewdness and your<char style="ord">i</char> cult prostitution.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said moreover unto me; Son of man, will you<char style="ord">i</char> judge Oholah <char style="add">[her own tent]</char> and Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char>? yes, declare unto them their abominations;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />That they have committed adultery, and blood <char style="add">[is]</char> in their hands, and with their idols have they committed adultery, and have also caused their sons, whom they bore unto me, to pass for them through <char style="add">[the fire]</char>, to devour <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Moreover this they have done unto me: they have defiled my Sanctuary in the same day, and have profaned my Shabbat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />For when they had slain their children to their idols, then they came the same day into my sanctuary to Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> it; and, lo, thus have they done in the midst of my house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And furthermore, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have sent for men to come from far, unto whom a messenger <char style="add">[was]</char> sent; and, lo, they came: for whom you<char style="ord">i</char> did wash yourself, painted your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and decked yourself with ornaments,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And sat upon a stately bed, and a table prepared before it, whereupon you<char style="ord">i</char> have set my incense and my oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And a voice of a multitude being at ease <char style="add">[was]</char> with her: and with the men of the common sort <char style="add">[were]</char> brought S’va <char style="add">[drunkards]</char> from the wilderness, which put bracelets upon their hands, and beautiful crowns upon their heads.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Then said I unto <char style="add">[her that was]</char> old in adulteries, Will they now commit cult prostitution with her, and she <char style="add">[with them]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />Yet they went in unto her, as they go in unto a woman that plays the prostitute: so went they in unto Oholah <char style="add">[her own tent]</char> and unto Oholivah <char style="add">[woman of the tent]</char>, the lewd women.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And the righteous men, they shall judge them after the manner of adulteresses, and after the manner of women that shed blood; because they <char style="add">[are]</char> adulteresses, and blood <char style="add">[is]</char> in their hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will bring up a company upon them, and will give them to be removed and spoiled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And the company shall stone them with stones, and dispatch them with their swords; they shall slay their sons and their daughters, and burn up their houses with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />Thus will I cause lewdness to cease out of the land, that all women may be taught not to do after your lewdness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And they shall recompense your lewdness upon you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall bear the sins of your idols: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Again in the ninth year, in the tenth month, in the tenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, write you<char style="ord">i</char> the name of the day, <char style="add">[even]</char> of this same day: the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> set himself against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> this same day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And utter a parable unto the rebellious house, and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Set on a pot, set <char style="add">[it]</char> on, and also pour water into it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Gather the pieces thereof into it, <char style="add">[even]</char> every good piece, the thigh, and the shoulder; fill <char style="add">[it]</char> with the choice bones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Take the choice of the flock, and burn also the bones under it, <char style="add">[and]</char> make it boil well, and let them seethe the bones of it in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For what reason thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Woe to the bloody city, to the pot whose scum <char style="add">[is]</char> in it, and whose scum is not gone out of it! bring it out piece by piece; let no lot fall upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For her blood is in the midst of her; she set it upon the top of a rock; she poured it not upon the ground, to cover it with dust;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />That it might cause fury to come up to take vengeance; I have set her blood upon the top of a rock, that it should not be covered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Woe to the bloody city! I will even make the pile for fire great.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Heap on wood, kindle the fire, consume the flesh, and spice it well, and let the bones be burned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then set it empty upon the coals thereof, that the brass of it may be hot, and may burn, and <char style="add">[that]</char> the filthiness of it may be molten in it, <char style="add">[that]</char> the scum of it may be consumed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />She has wearied <char style="add">[herself]</char> with lies, and her great scum went not forth out of her: her scum <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in the fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />In your<char style="ord">i</char> filthiness <char style="add">[is]</char> lewdness: because I have purged you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> were not purged, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not be purged from your<char style="ord">i</char> filthiness any more, till I have caused my fury to rest upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>: it shall come to pass, and I will do <char style="add">[it]</char>; I will not go back, neither will I spare, neither will I repent; according to your<char style="ord">i</char> ways, and according to your<char style="ord">i</char> doings, shall they judge you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Also the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Son of man, behold, I take away from you<char style="ord">i</char> the desire of your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes with a stroke: yet neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> mourn nor weep, neither shall your<char style="ord">i</char> tears run down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char> to cry, make no mourning for the dead, bind the tire of your<char style="ord">i</char> head upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and put on your<char style="ord">i</char> shoes upon your<char style="ord">i</char> feet, and cover not <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> lips, and eat not the bread of men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />So I spoke unto the people in the morning: and at even my wife died; and I did in the morning as I was commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the people said unto me, Will you<char style="ord">i</char> not tell us what these <char style="add">[things are]</char> to us, that you<char style="ord">i</char> do <char style="add">[so]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then I answered them, The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Speak unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> my sanctuary, the excellency of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and that which your soul pities; and your sons and your daughters whom you<char style="ord">2f</char> have left shall fall by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do as I have done: you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not cover <char style="add">[your]</char> lips, nor eat the bread of men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And your tires <char style="add">[shall be]</char> upon your heads, and your shoes upon your feet: you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not mourn nor weep; but you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall pine away for your iniquities, and mourn one toward another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Thus Yechezk’el <char style="add">[God strengthens]</char> is unto you a sign: according to all that he has done shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> do: and when this comes, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Also, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, <char style="add">[shall it]</char> not <char style="add">[be]</char> in the day when I take from them their strength, the joy of their glory, the desire of their eyes, and that whereupon they set their minds, their sons and their daughters,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> he that escapes in that day shall come unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, to cause <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> to hear <char style="add">[it]</char> with <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> ears?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />In that day shall your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth be opened to him which is escaped, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak, and be no more dumb: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be a sign unto them; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and prophesy against them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say unto the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, Hear the word of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> said, Aha, against my sanctuary, when it was profaned; and against the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when it was desolate; and against the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, when they went into captivity;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Behold, therefore I will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> to the men of the east for a possession, and they shall set their palaces in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and make their dwellings in you<char style="ord">i</char>: they shall eat your<char style="ord">i</char> fruit, and they shall drink your<char style="ord">i</char> milk.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I will make Rabbah <char style="add">[Great]</char> a stable for camels, and the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> a couchingplace for flocks: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have clapped <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hands, and stamped with the feet, and rejoiced in heart with all your<char style="ord">i</char> despite <char style="pn">(contempt; angy hatred)</char> against the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Behold, therefore I will stretch out my hand upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will deliver you<char style="ord">i</char> for a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> to the heathen; and I will cut you<char style="ord">i</char> off from the people, and I will cause you<char style="ord">i</char> to perish out of the countries: I will destroy you<char style="ord">i</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because that Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> and Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char> do say, Behold, the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [is]</char> like unto all the heathen;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Therefore, behold, I will open the side of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> from the cities, from his cities <char style="add">[which are]</char> on his frontiers, the glory of the country, Beit-Yeshimot <char style="add">[House of the Desolation]</char>, Ba’al-M’on <char style="add">[lord of the Habitation]</char>, and Kiryatayim <char style="add">[two cities]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Unto the men of the east with the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and will give them in possession, that the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> may not be remembered among the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I will execute judgments upon Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because that Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> has dealt against the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> by taking vengeance, and has greatly offended, and revenged himself upon them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will also stretch out my hand upon Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and will cut off man and beast from it; and I will make it desolate from Teman <char style="add">[south]</char>; and they of D’dan <char style="add">[low country]</char> shall fall by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will lay my vengeance upon Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> by the hand of my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and they shall do in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char> according to my anger and according to my fury; and they shall know my vengeance, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> have dealt by revenge, and have taken vengeance with a despiteful heart, to destroy <char style="add">[it]</char> for the old hatred;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will stretch out my hand upon the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and I will cut off the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and destroy the remnant of the sea coast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And I will execute great vengeance upon them with furious rebukes; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I shall lay my vengeance upon them.</para>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, because that Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> has said against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, Aha, she is broken <char style="add">[that was]</char> the gates of the people: she is turned unto me: I shall be replenished, <char style="add">[now]</char> she is laid waste:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and will cause many nations to come up against you<char style="ord">i</char>, as the sea causes his waves to come up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they shall destroy the walls of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and break down her towers: I will also scrape her dust from her, and make her like the top of a rock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />It shall be <char style="add">[a place for]</char> the spreading of nets in the midst of the sea: for I have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: and it shall become a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> to the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And her daughters which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the field shall be slain by the sword; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will bring upon Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> N’vukhadretzar <char style="add">[may Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, a king of kings, from the north, with horses, and with chariots, and with horsemen, and companies, and much people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He shall slay with the sword your<char style="ord">i</char> daughters in the field: and he shall make a fort against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and cast a mount against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and lift up the buckler <char style="pn">(round shielf held with a grip)</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he shall set engines of war against you<char style="ord">i</char> walls, and with his axes he shall break down your<char style="ord">i</char> towers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />By reason of the abundance of his horses their dust shall cover you<char style="ord">i</char>: your<char style="ord">i</char> walls shall shake at the noise of the horsemen, and of the wheels, and of the chariots, when he shall enter into your<char style="ord">i</char> gates, as men enter into a city wherein is made a breach <char style="pn">(breaking forth; a break; opening, inlet)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />With the hoofs of his horses shall he trample down all your<char style="ord">i</char> streets: he shall slay your<char style="ord">i</char> people by the sword, and your<char style="ord">i</char> strong garrisons shall go down to the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they shall make a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of your<char style="ord">i</char> riches, and make a prey of your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise: and they shall break down your<char style="ord">i</char> walls, and destroy you<char style="ord">i</char> pleasant houses: and they shall lay your<char style="ord">i</char> stones and your<char style="ord">i</char> timber and your<char style="ord">i</char> dust in the midst of the water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I will cause the noise of your<char style="ord">i</char> songs to cease; and the sound of your<char style="ord">i</char> harps shall be no more heard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> like the top of a rock: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be <char style="add">[a place]</char> to spread nets upon; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be built no more: for I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> to Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>; Shall not the isles shake at the sound of your<char style="ord">i</char> fall, when the wounded cry, when the slaughter is made in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then all the princes of the sea shall come down from their thrones, and lay away their robes, and put off their adorned with needlework garments: they shall clothe themselves with trembling; they shall sit upon the ground, and shall tremble at <char style="add">[every]</char> moment, and be astonished at you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they shall take up a lamentation for you<char style="ord">i</char>, and say to you<char style="ord">i</char>, How are you<char style="ord">i</char> destroyed, <char style="add">[that were]</char> inhabited of seafaring men, the renowned city, which were strong in the sea, she and her inhabitants, which cause their terror <char style="add">[to be]</char> on all that haunt <char style="pn">(where one goes freequently)</char> it!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now shall the isles tremble in the day of your<char style="ord">i</char> fall; yes, the isles that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the sea shall be troubled at your<char style="ord">i</char> departure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; When I shall make you<char style="ord">i</char> a desolate city, like the cities that are not inhabited; when I shall bring up the deep upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and great waters shall cover you<char style="ord">i</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />When I shall bring you<char style="ord">i</char> down with them that descend into the pit, with the people of old time, and shall set you<char style="ord">i</char> in the low parts of the earth, in places desolate of old, with them that go down to the pit, that you<char style="ord">i</char> be not inhabited; and I shall set glory in the land of the living;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> a terror, and you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> no <char style="add">[more]</char>: though you<char style="ord">i</char> be sought for, yet shall you<char style="ord">i</char> never be found again, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Now, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, take up a lamentation for Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say unto Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, O you<char style="ord">i</char> that are situate at the entry of the sea, <char style="add">[which are]</char> a merchant of the people for many isles, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; O Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> have said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> of perfect beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> borders <char style="add">[are]</char> in the midst of the seas, your<char style="ord">i</char> builders have perfected your<char style="ord">i</char> beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />They have made all your<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[ship]</char> boards of fir trees of S’nir <char style="add">[snow mountain]</char>: they have taken cedars from L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> to make masts for you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Of]</char> the oaks of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char> have they made your<char style="ord">i</char> oars; the company of the Ashuri <char style="add">[guided; Blessed (Favored by God; happy; prosperous)]</char> have made your<char style="ord">i</char> benches <char style="add">[of]</char> ivory, <char style="add">[brought]</char> out of the isles of Kittim <char style="add">[Bruisers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Fine linen with adorned with needlework work from Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> was that which you<char style="ord">i</char> spread forth to be your<char style="ord">i</char> sail; blue and purple from the isles of Elishah <char style="add">[God of the coming one]</char> was that which covered you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The inhabitants of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char> and Arvad <char style="add">[I shall break loose]</char> were your<char style="ord">i</char> mariners: your<char style="ord">i</char> wise <char style="add">[men]</char>, O Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> were in you<char style="ord">i</char>, were your<char style="ord">i</char> pilots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The ancients of G’val <char style="add">[mountain]</char> and the wise <char style="add">[men]</char> thereof were in you<char style="ord">i</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> caulkers: all the ships of the sea with their mariners were in you<char style="ord">i</char> to occupy your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />They of Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char> and of Lud <char style="add">[strife]</char> and of Put <char style="add">[a bow]</char> were in you<char style="ord">i</char> army, your<char style="ord">i</char> men of war: they hanged the shield and helmet in you<char style="ord">i</char>; they set forth your<char style="ord">i</char> comeliness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The men of Arvad <char style="add">[I shall break loose]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> army <char style="add">[were]</char> upon your<char style="ord">i</char> walls round about, and the Gamadim <char style="add">[warriors]</char> were in your<char style="ord">i</char> towers: they hanged their shields upon your<char style="ord">i</char> walls round about; they have made your<char style="ord">i</char> beauty perfect.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper] [was]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchant by reason of the multitude of all <char style="add">[kind of]</char> riches; with silver, iron, tin, and lead, they traded in your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yavan <char style="pn">(Greece)</char> <char style="add">[Ionia]</char>, Tuval <char style="add">[you shall be brought]</char>, and Meshekh <char style="add">[drawing out]</char>, they <char style="add">[were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants: they traded the persons of men and vessels of brass in your<char style="ord">i</char> market.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />They of the house of Togarmah <char style="add">[you will break her]</char> traded in your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char> with horses and horsemen and mules.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The men of D’dan <char style="add">[low country] [were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants; many isles <char style="add">[were]</char> the merchandise of you<char style="ord">i</char> hand: they brought you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[for]</char> a present horns of ivory and ebony.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted] [was]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchant by reason of the multitude of the wares of your<char style="ord">i</char> making: they occupied in your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char> with emeralds, purple, and adorned with needlework work, and fine linen, and coral, and agate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, they <char style="add">[were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants: they traded in your<char style="ord">i</char> market wheat of Minnit <char style="add">[distribution]</char>, and cakes, and honey, and oil, and balm <char style="pn">(a medicine; rosin from a bush)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver] [was]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchant in the multitude of the wares of your<char style="ord">i</char> making, for the multitude of all riches; in the wine of Helbon <char style="add">[fertile]</char>, and white wool.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> also and Yavan <char style="pn">(Greece)</char> <char style="add">[Ionia]</char> going to and fro occupied in your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char>: bright iron, cassia, and calamus, were in your<char style="ord">i</char> market.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />D’dan <char style="add">[low country] [was]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchant in precious clothes for chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Arabia <char style="add">[steppe-dwellers]</char>, and all the princes of Kedar <char style="add">[dark]</char>, they occupied with your<char style="ord">i</char> in lambs, and rams, and goats: in these <char style="add">[were they]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />The merchants of Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char> and Ra’mah <char style="add">[horse’s mane]</char>, they <char style="add">[were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants: they occupied in your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char> with chief of all spices, and with all precious stones, and gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Haran <char style="add">[mountaineer]</char>, and Kaneh <char style="add">[to give a flattering title]</char>, and ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>, the merchants of Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char>, Ashur <char style="add">[A Level Plain]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> Kilmad <char style="add">[enclosure]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />These <char style="add">[were]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> merchants in all sorts <char style="add">[of things]</char>, in blue clothes, and adorned with needlework work, and in chests of rich apparel, bound with cords, and made of cedar, among your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />The ships of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char> did sing of you<char style="ord">i</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> market: and you<char style="ord">i</char> were replenished, and made very glorious in the midst of the seas.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> rowers have brought you<char style="ord">i</char> into great waters: the east wind has broken you<char style="ord">i</char> in the midst of the seas.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> riches, and your<char style="ord">i</char> wares <char style="pn">(something gotten at the fair)</char>, your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise, your<char style="ord">i</char> mariners, and your<char style="ord">i</char> pilots, your<char style="ord">i</char> caulkers, and the occupiers of your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise, and all your<char style="ord">i</char> men of war, that <char style="add">[are]</char> in you<char style="ord">i</char>, and in all your<char style="ord">i</char> company which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>, shall fall into the midst of the seas in the day of your<char style="ord">i</char> ruin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />The suburbs shall shake at the sound of the cry of your<char style="ord">i</char> pilots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And all that handle the oar, the mariners, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the pilots of the sea, shall come down from their ships, they shall stand upon the land;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And shall cause their voice to be heard against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and shall cry bitterly, and shall cast up dust upon their heads, they shall wallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> themselves in the ashes:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And they shall make themselves utterly bald for you<char style="ord">i</char>, and gird them with sackcloth, and they shall weep for you<char style="ord">i</char> with bitterness of heart <char style="add">[and]</char> bitter wailing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And in their wailing they shall take up a lamentation for you<char style="ord">i</char>, and lament over you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, What <char style="add">[city is]</char> like Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, like the destroyed in the midst of the sea?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />When your<char style="ord">i</char> wares went forth out of the seas, you<char style="ord">i</char> filled many people; you<char style="ord">i</char> did enrich the kings of the earth with the multitude of your<char style="ord">i</char> riches and of your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />In the time <char style="add">[when]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be broken by the seas in the depths of the waters your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise and all your<char style="ord">i</char> company in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> shall fall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />All the inhabitants of the isles shall be astonished at you<char style="ord">i</char>, and their kings shall be sore afraid, they shall be troubled in <char style="add">[their]</char> Countenance <char style="pn">(Face, appearance; show favor)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />The merchants among the people shall hiss at you<char style="ord">i</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be a terror, and never <char style="add">[shall be]</char> any more.</para>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, say unto the prince of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because your<char style="ord">i</char> heart <char style="add">[is]</char> lifted up, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have said, I <char style="add">[am]</char> a God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, I sit <char style="add">[in]</char> the seat of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, in the midst of the seas; yet you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a man, and not God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, though you<char style="ord">i</char> set your<char style="ord">i</char> heart as the heart of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> wiser than Dani’el <char style="add">[God is Judge]</char>; there is no secret that they can hide from you<char style="ord">i</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />With your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom and with your<char style="ord">i</char> understanding you<char style="ord">i</char> have gotten you<char style="ord">i</char> riches, and have gotten gold and silver into your<char style="ord">i</char> treasures:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />By your<char style="ord">i</char> great wisdom <char style="add">[and]</char> by your<char style="ord">i</char> traffick <char style="pn">(trade; do business)</char> have you<char style="ord">i</char> increased your<char style="ord">i</char> riches, and your<char style="ord">i</char> heart is lifted up because of your<char style="ord">i</char> riches:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have set your<char style="ord">i</char> heart as the heart of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Behold, therefore I will bring strangers upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, the terrible of the nations: and they shall draw their swords against the beauty of your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom, and they shall defile your<char style="ord">i</char> brightness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />They shall bring you<char style="ord">i</char> down to the pit, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die the deaths of <char style="add">[them that are]</char> slain in the midst of the seas.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Will you<char style="ord">i</char> yet say before him that slays you<char style="ord">i</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>? but you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a man, and no God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, in the hand of him that slays you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall die the deaths of the uncircumcised by the hand of strangers: for I have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Son of man, take up a lamentation upon the king of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and say unto him, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> seal up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have been in ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char> the garden of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; every precious stone <char style="add">[was]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the Carbuncle <char style="pn">(a red precious stone)</char>, and gold: the workmanship of your<char style="ord">i</char> tambourines and of your<char style="ord">i</char> pipes was prepared in you<char style="ord">i</char> in the day that you<char style="ord">i</char> were created.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the anointed cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> that covers; and I have set you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[so]</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> were upon the holy mountain of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; you<char style="ord">i</char> have walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> perfect in your<char style="ord">i</char> ways from the day that you<char style="ord">i</char> were created, till iniquity was found in you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />By the multitude of your<char style="ord">i</char> merchandise they have filled the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char> with violence, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have sinned: therefore I will cast you<char style="ord">i</char> as Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> out of the mountain of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and I will destroy you<char style="ord">i</char>, O covering cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, from the midst of the stones of fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> heart was lifted up because of your<char style="ord">i</char> beauty, you<char style="ord">i</char> have corrupted your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom by reason of your<char style="ord">i</char> brightness: I will cast you<char style="ord">i</char> to the ground, I will lay you<char style="ord">i</char> before kings, that they may behold you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> have defiled your<char style="ord">i</char> sanctuaries by the multitude of your<char style="ord">i</char> iniquities, by the iniquity of your<char style="ord">i</char> traffick <char style="pn">(trade; do business)</char>; therefore will I bring forth a fire from the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>, it shall devour you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> to ashes upon the earth in the sight of all them that behold you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />All they that know you<char style="ord">i</char> among the people shall be astonished at you<char style="ord">i</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be a terror, and never <char style="add">[shall]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and prophesy against it,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>; and I will be glorified in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I shall have executed judgments in her, and shall be sanctified in her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For I will send into her pestilence, and blood into her streets; and the wounded shall be judged in the midst of her by the sword upon her on every side; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And there shall be no more a pricking brier unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, nor <char style="add">[any]</char> grieving thorn of all <char style="add">[that are]</char> round about them, that despised them; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; When I shall have gathered the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the people among whom they are scattered, and shall be sanctified in them in the sight of the heathen, then shall they dwell in their land that I have given to my servant Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And they shall dwell safely in it, and shall build houses, and plant vineyards; yes, they shall dwell with confidence, when I have executed judgments upon all those that despise them round about them; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the tenth year, in the tenth <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the twelfth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and prophesy against him, and against all Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Speak, and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, the great dragon that lies in the midst of his rivers, which has said, My river <char style="add">[is]</char> my own, and I have made <char style="add">[it]</char> for myself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But I will put hooks in your<char style="ord">i</char> jaws, and I will cause the fish of your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers to stick unto your<char style="ord">i</char> scales, and I will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> up out of the midst of your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers, and all the fish of your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers shall stick unto your<char style="ord">i</char> scales.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I will leave you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[thrown]</char> into the wilderness, you<char style="ord">i</char> and all the fish of your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall fall upon the open fields; you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not be brought together, nor gathered: I have given you<char style="ord">i</char> for meat to the beasts of the field and to the fowls of the heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And all the inhabitants of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, because they have been a staff of reed to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />When they took hold of you<char style="ord">i</char> by your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, you<char style="ord">i</char> did break, and rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> all their shoulder: and when they leaned upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> broke, and made all their waist to be at a stand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will bring a sword upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and cut off man and beast out of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> shall be desolate and waste; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: because he has said, The river <char style="add">[is]</char> my, and I have made <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Behold, therefore I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and against your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers, and I will make the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> utterly waste <char style="add">[and]</char> desolate, from the tower of S’venah <char style="add">[meaning disputed]</char> even unto the border of Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />No foot of man shall pass through it, nor foot of beast shall pass through it, neither shall it be inhabited forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I will make the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> desolate in the midst of the countries <char style="add">[that are]</char> desolate, and her cities among the cities <char style="add">[that are]</char> laid waste shall be desolate forty years: and I will scatter the Mitzri among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yet thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; At the end of forty years will I gather the Mitzri from the people to which they were scattered:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will bring again the captivity of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and will cause them to return <char style="add">[into]</char> the land of Patros <char style="add">[region of the south]</char>, into the land of their habitation; and they shall be there a humble kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />It shall be the basest of the kingdoms; neither shall it exalt itself any more above the nations: for I will diminish them, that they shall no more rule over the nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it shall be no more the confidence of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which brings <char style="add">[their]</char> iniquity to remembrance, when they shall look after them: but they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass in the seven and twentieth year, in the first <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Son of man, N’vukhadretzar <char style="add">[may Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> caused his army to serve a great service against Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>: every head <char style="add">[was]</char> made bald, and every shoulder <char style="add">[was]</char> smooth <char style="pn">(bare; bald)</char>: yet had he no wages, nor his army, for Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, for the service that he had served against it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will give the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> unto N’vukhadretzar <char style="add">[may Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>; and he shall take her multitude, and take her spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and take her prey; and it shall be the wages for his army.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />I have given him the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place] [for]</char> his labour which he served against it, because they wrought for me, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />In that day will I cause the horn of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to bud forth, and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> the opening of the mouth in the midst of them; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, prophesy and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Howl you<char style="ord">2f</char>, Woe worth the day!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For the day <char style="add">[is]</char> near, even the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> near, a cloudy day; it shall be the time of the heathen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the sword shall come upon Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and great pain shall be in Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char>, when the slain shall fall in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and they shall take away her multitude, and her foundations shall be broken down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char>, and Libya <char style="pn">(Put)</char> <char style="add">[a bow]</char>, and Lydia <char style="pn">(Lud)</char> <char style="add">[strife]</char>, and all the mingled people, and Kuv <char style="add">[meaning unknown]</char>, and the men of the land that is in league, shall fall with them by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; They also that uphold Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> shall fall; and the pride of her power shall come down: from the tower of S’venah <char style="add">[meaning disputed]</char> shall they fall in it by the sword, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And they shall be desolate in the midst of the countries <char style="add">[that are]</char> desolate, and her cities shall be in the midst of the cities <char style="add">[that are]</char> wasted.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have set a fire in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and <char style="add">[when]</char> all her helpers shall be destroyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />In that day shall messengers go forth from me in ships to make the careless Ethiopians afraid, and great pain shall come upon them, as in the day of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: for, lo, it comes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will also make the multitude of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> to cease by the hand of N’vukhadretzar <char style="add">[may Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />He and his people with him, the terrible of the nations, shall be brought to destroy the land: and they shall draw their swords against Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and fill the land with the slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I will make the rivers dry, and sell the land into the hand of the wicked: and I will make the land waste, and all that is in it, by the hand of strangers: I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will also destroy the idols, and I will cause <char style="add">[their]</char> images to cease out of Nof <char style="add">[presentability]</char>; and there shall be no more a prince of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: and I will put a fear in the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And I will make Patros <char style="add">[region of the south]</char> desolate, and will set fire in Tzo’an <char style="add">[Place of Departure]</char>, and will execute judgments in No.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And I will pour my fury upon Seen <char style="add">[thorn]</char>, the strength of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; and I will cut off the multitude of No.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And I will set fire in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: Sin shall have great pain, and No shall be rent asunder, and Nof <char style="add">[presentability] [shall have]</char> distresses daily.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />The young men of On <char style="add">[vanity]</char> and of Pi-Veset <char style="add">[mouth of loathing]</char> shall fall by the sword: and these <char style="add">[cities]</char> shall go into captivity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />At T’chafin’ches <char style="add">[you will fill hands with pity]</char> also the day shall be darkened, when I shall break there the yokes of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: and the pomp of her strength shall cease in her: as for her, a cloud shall cover her, and her daughters shall go into captivity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Thus will I execute judgments in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the seventh <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Son of man, I have broken the arm of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; and, lo, it shall not be bound up to be healed, to put a roller to bind it, to make it strong to hold the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and will break his arms, the strong, and that which was broken; and I will cause the sword to fall out of his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I will scatter the Mitzri among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and put my sword in his hand: but I will break Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> arms, and he shall groan before him with the groanings of a deadly wounded <char style="add">[man]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But I will strengthen the arms of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and the arms of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> shall fall down; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I shall put my sword into the hand of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and he shall stretch it out upon the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And I will scatter the Mitzri among the nations, and disperse them among the countries; and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the third <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, speak unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and to his multitude; Whom are you<char style="ord">i</char> like in you<char style="ord">i</char> greatness?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, the Ashur <char style="pn">(Assyrian)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> a cedar in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> with fair branches, and with a shadowing shroud, and of an high stature; and his top was among the thick boughs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The waters made him great, the deep set him up on high with her rivers running round about his plants, and sent out her little rivers unto all the trees of the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Therefore his height was exalted above all the trees of the field, and his boughs were multiplied, and his branches became long because of the multitude of waters, when he shot forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />All the fowls of heaven made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches did all the beasts of the field bring forth their young, and under his shadow dwelt all great nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus was he fair in his greatness, in the length of his branches: for his root was by great waters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The cedars in the garden of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> could not hide him: the fir trees were not like his boughs, and the chestnut trees were not like his branches; nor any tree in the garden of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was like unto him in his beauty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />I have made him fair by the multitude of his branches: so that all the trees of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>, that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the garden of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, envied him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have lifted up yourself in height, and he has shot up his top among the thick boughs, and his heart is lifted up in his height;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />I have therefore delivered him into the hand of the mighty one of the heathen; he shall surely deal with him: I have driven him out for his wickedness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And strangers, the terrible of the nations, have cut him off, and have left him: upon the mountains and in all the valleys his branches are fallen, and his boughs are broken by all the rivers of the land; and all the people of the earth are gone down from his shadow, and have left him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Upon his ruin shall all the fowls of the heaven remain, and all the beasts of the field shall be upon his branches:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />To the end that none of all the trees by the waters exalt themselves for their height, neither shoot up their top among the thick boughs, neither their trees stand up in their height, all that drink water: for they are all delivered unto death, to the lower parts of the earth, in the midst of the children of men, with them that go down to the pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; In the day when he went down to the grave I caused a mourning: I covered the deep for him, and I restrained the floods thereof, and the great waters were detained <char style="pn">(held)</char>: and I caused L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> to mourn for him, and all the trees of the field fainted for him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />I made the nations to shake at the sound of his fall, when I cast him down to hell with them that descend into the pit: and all the trees of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>, the choice and best of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, all that drink water, shall be comforted in the lower parts of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />They also went down into hell with him unto <char style="add">[them that be]</char> slain with the sword; and <char style="add">[they that were]</char> his arm, <char style="add">[that]</char> dwelt under his shadow in the midst of the heathen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />To whom are you<char style="ord">i</char> thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>? yet shall you<char style="ord">i</char> be brought down with the trees of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char> unto the lower parts of the earth: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall lie in the midst of the uncircumcised with <char style="add">[them that be]</char> slain by the sword. This <char style="add">[is]</char> Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> and all his multitude, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="32" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, take up a lamentation for Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and say unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> are like a young lion of the nations, and you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> as a whale in the seas: and you<char style="ord">i</char> came forth with your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers, and troubled the waters with your<char style="ord">i</char> feet, and fouled their rivers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will therefore spread out my net over you<char style="ord">i</char> with a company of many people; and they shall bring you<char style="ord">i</char> up in my net.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then will I leave you<char style="ord">i</char> upon the land, I will cast you<char style="ord">i</char> forth upon the open field, and will cause all the fowls of the heaven to remain upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will fill the beasts of the whole earth with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I will lay your<char style="ord">i</char> flesh upon the mountains, and fill the valleys with your<char style="ord">i</char> height.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />I will also water with your<char style="ord">i</char> blood the land wherein you<char style="ord">i</char> swim, <char style="add">[even]</char> to the mountains; and the rivers shall be full of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when I shall put you<char style="ord">i</char> out, I will cover the heaven, and make the stars thereof dark; I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon shall not give her light.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />All the bright lights of heaven will I make dark over you<char style="ord">i</char>, and set darkness upon your<char style="ord">i</char> land, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />I will also vex the hearts of many people, when I shall bring your<char style="ord">i</char> destruction among the nations, into the countries which you<char style="ord">i</char> have not known.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Yes, I will make many people amazed at you<char style="ord">i</char>, and their kings shall be horribly afraid for you<char style="ord">i</char>, when I shall brandish my sword before them; and they shall tremble at <char style="add">[every]</char> moment, every man for his own life, in the day of your<char style="ord">i</char> fall.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; The sword of the king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char> shall come upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />By the swords of the mighty will I cause your<char style="ord">i</char> multitude to fall, the terrible of the nations, all of them: and they shall spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> the pomp of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and all the multitude thereof shall be destroyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />I will destroy also all the beasts thereof from beside the great waters; neither shall the foot of man trouble them anymore, nor the hoofs of beasts trouble them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then will I make their waters deep, and cause their rivers to run like oil, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />When I shall make the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> desolate, and the country shall be destitute of that whereof it was full, when I shall strike all them that dwell in it, then shall they know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the lamentation which they shall lament her: the daughters of the nations shall lament her: they shall lament for her, <char style="add">[even]</char> for Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and for all her multitude, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />It came to pass also in the twelfth year, in the fifteenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Son of man, wail for the multitude of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and cast them down, <char style="add">[even]</char> her, and the daughters of the famous nations, unto the lower parts of the earth, with them that go down into the pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Whom do you<char style="ord">i</char> pass in beauty? go down, and be you<char style="ord">i</char> laid with the uncircumcised.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />They shall fall in the midst of <char style="add">[them that are]</char> slain by the sword: she is delivered to the sword: draw her and all her multitudes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The strong among the mighty shall speak to him out of the midst of hell with them that help him: they are gone down, they lie uncircumcised, slain by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Ashur <char style="add">[A Level Plain] [is]</char> there and all her company: his graves <char style="add">[are]</char> about him: all of them slain, fallen by the sword:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Whose graves are set in the sides of the pit, and her company is round about her grave: all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which caused terror in the land of the living.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />There <char style="add">[is]</char> ‘Eilam <char style="add">[eternity]</char> and all her multitude round about her grave, all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which are gone down uncircumcised into the lower parts of the earth, which caused their terror in the land of the living; yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />They have set her a bed in the midst of the slain with all her multitude: her graves <char style="add">[are]</char> round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword: though their terror was caused in the land of the living, yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit: he is put in the midst of <char style="add">[them that be]</char> slain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />There <char style="add">[is]</char> Meshekh <char style="add">[drawing out]</char>, Tuval <char style="add">[you shall be brought]</char>, and all her multitude: her graves <char style="add">[are]</char> round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword, though they caused their terror in the land of the living.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And they shall not lie with the mighty <char style="add">[that are]</char> fallen of the uncircumcised, which are gone down to hell with their weapons of war: and they have laid their swords under their heads, but their iniquities shall be upon their bones, though <char style="add">[they were]</char> the terror of the mighty in the land of the living.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Yes, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be broken in the midst of the uncircumcised, and shall lie with <char style="add">[them that are]</char> slain with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />There <char style="add">[is]</char> Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, her kings, and all her princes, which with their might are laid by <char style="add">[them that were]</char> slain by the sword: they shall lie with the uncircumcised, and with them that go down to the pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />There <char style="add">[be]</char> the princes of the north, all of them, and all the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, which are gone down with the slain; with their terror they are ashamed of their might; and they lie uncircumcised with <char style="add">[them that be]</char> slain by the sword, and bear their shame with them that go down to the pit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> shall see them, and shall be comforted over all his multitude, <char style="add">[even]</char> Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> and all his army slain by the sword, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />For I have caused my terror in the land of the living: and he shall be laid in the midst of the uncircumcised with <char style="add">[them that are]</char> slain with the sword, <char style="add">[even]</char> Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> and all his multitude, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="33" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, speak to the children of your<char style="ord">i</char> people, and say unto them, When I bring the sword upon a land, if the people of the land take a man of their coasts, and set him for their watchman:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />If when he sees the sword come upon the land, he blow the trumpet, and warn the people;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then whosoever hears the sound of the trumpet, and takes not warning; if the sword come, and take him away, his blood shall be upon his own head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He heard the sound of the trumpet, and took not warning; his blood shall be upon him. But he that takes warning shall deliver his soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But if the watchman see the sword come, and blow not the trumpet, and the people be not warned; if the sword come, and take <char style="add">[any]</char> person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at the watchman’s hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Son of man, I have set you<char style="ord">i</char> a watchman unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall hear the word at my mouth, and warn them from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />When I say unto the wicked, O wicked <char style="add">[man]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die; if you<char style="ord">i</char> do not speak to warn the wicked from his way, that wicked <char style="add">[man]</char> shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Nevertheless, if you<char style="ord">i</char> warn the wicked of his way to turn from it; if he do not turn from his way, he shall die in his iniquity; but you<char style="ord">i</char> have delivered your<char style="ord">i</char> soul.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore, O you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, speak unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; Thus you<char style="ord">2f</char> speak, saying, If our transgressions and our sins <char style="add">[be]</char> upon us, and we pine away in them, how should we then live?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Say unto them, <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn you<char style="ord">2f</char>, turn you<char style="ord">2f</char> from your evil ways; for why will you<char style="ord">2f</char> die, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Therefore, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, say unto the children of your<char style="ord">i</char> people, The righteousness of the righteous shall not deliver him in the day of his transgression: as for the wickedness of the wicked, he shall not fall thereby in the day that he turns from his wickedness; neither shall the righteous be able to live for his <char style="add">[righteousness]</char> in the day that he sins.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />When I shall say to the righteous, <char style="add">[that]</char> he shall surely live; if he trust to his own righteousness, and commit iniquity, all his righteousnesses shall not be remembered; but for his iniquity that he has committed, he shall die for it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Again, when I say unto the wicked, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die; if he turn from his sin, and do that which is lawful and right;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[If]</char> the wicked restore the pledge, give again that he had robbed, walk in the statutes of life, without committing iniquity; he shall surely live, he shall not die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />None of his sins that he has committed shall be mentioned unto him: he has done that which is lawful and right; he shall surely live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Yet the children of you<char style="ord">i</char> people say, The way of the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> is not equal: but as for them, their way is not equal.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />When the righteous turns from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, he shall even die thereby.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But if the wicked turn from his wickedness, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall live thereby.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">2f</char> say, The way of the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> is not equal. O you<char style="ord">2f</char> house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I will judge you everyone after his ways.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And it came to pass in the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the fifth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, <char style="add">[that]</char> one that had escaped out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> came unto me, saying, The city is smitten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was upon me in the evening, afore he that was escaped came; and had opened my mouth, until he came to me in the morning; and my mouth was opened, and I was no more dumb.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Son of man, they that inhabit those wastes of the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> speak, saying, Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char> was one, and he inherited the land: but we <char style="add">[are]</char> many; the land is given us for inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />For what reason say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; You<char style="ord">2f</char> eat with the blood, and lift up your eyes toward your idols, and shed blood: and shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> possess the land?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> stand upon your sword, you<char style="ord">2f</char> work abomination, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> defile everyone his neighbour’s wife: and shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> possess the land?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Say you<char style="ord">i</char> thus unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, surely they that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the wastes shall fall by the sword, and him that <char style="add">[is]</char> in the open field will I give to the beasts to be devoured, and they that <char style="add">[be]</char> in the forts and in the caves shall die of the pestilence.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />For I will lay the land most desolate, and the pomp of her strength shall cease; and the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be desolate, that none shall pass through.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then shall they know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have laid the land most desolate because of all their abominations which they have committed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Also, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, the children of you<char style="ord">i</char> people still are talking against you<char style="ord">i</char> by the walls and in the doors of the houses, and speak one to another, everyone to his brother, saying, Come, I pray you, and hear what is the word that comes forth from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And they come unto you<char style="ord">i</char> as the people comes, and they sit before you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[as]</char> my people, and they hear your<char style="ord">i</char> words, but they will not do them: for with their mouth they show much love, <char style="add">[but]</char> their heart goes after their covetousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And, lo, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> unto them as a very lovely song of one that has a pleasant voice, and can play well on an instrument: for they hear your<char style="ord">i</char> words, but they do them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And when this comes to pass, <char style="pn">(lo, it will come,)</char> then shall they know that a prophet has been among them.</para>
  <chapter number="34" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, prophesy, and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> unto the shepherds; Woe <char style="add">[be]</char> to the shepherds of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> eat the fat, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> clothe you with the wool, you<char style="ord">2f</char> kill them that are fed: <char style="add">[but]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> feed not the flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The diseased have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not strengthened, neither have you<char style="ord">2f</char> healed that which was sick, neither have you<char style="ord">2f</char> bound up <char style="add">[that which was]</char> broken, neither have you<char style="ord">2f</char> brought again that which was driven away, neither have you<char style="ord">2f</char> sought that which was lost; but with force and with cruelty have you<char style="ord">2f</char> ruled them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they were scattered, because <char style="add">[there is]</char> no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />My sheep wandered through all the mountains, and upon every high hill: yes, my flock was scattered upon all the face of the earth, and none did search or seek <char style="add">[after them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shepherds, hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, surely because my flock became a prey, and my flock became meat to every beast of the field, because <char style="add">[there was]</char> no shepherd, neither did my shepherds search for my flock, but the shepherds fed themselves, and fed not my flock;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Therefore, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> shepherds, hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock; neither shall the shepherds feed themselves anymore; for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />As a shepherd seeks out his flock in the day that he is among his sheep <char style="add">[that are]</char> scattered; so will I seek out my sheep, and will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I will bring them out from the people, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them to their own land, and feed them upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by the rivers, and in all the inhabited places of the country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />I will feed them in a good pasture, and upon the high mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall their fold be: there shall they lie in a good fold, and <char style="add">[in]</char> a fat pasture shall they feed upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />I will feed my flock, and I will cause them to lie down, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up <char style="add">[that which was]</char> broken, and will strengthen that which was sick: but I will destroy the fat and the strong; I will feed them with judgment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> you, O my flock, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I judge between cattle and cattle, between the rams and the he goats.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Seem it]</char> a small thing unto you to have eaten up the good pasture, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> must trample down with your feet the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of your pastures? and to have drunk of the deep waters, but you<char style="ord">2f</char> must foul the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> with your feet?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And <char style="add">[as for]</char> my flock, they eat that which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have trampled with your feet; and they drink that which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have fouled with your feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> unto them; Behold, I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I, will judge between the fat cattle and between the lean cattle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have thrust with side and with shoulder, and pushed all the diseased with your horns, till you<char style="ord">2f</char> have scattered them abroad;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Therefore will I save my flock, and they shall no more be a prey; and I will judge between cattle and cattle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, <char style="add">[even]</char> my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> a prince among them; I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And I will make with them a covenant of peace, and will cause the evil beasts to cease out of the land: and they shall dwell safely in the wilderness, and sleep in the woods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And I will make them and the places round about my hill a blessing; and I will cause the shower to come down in his season; there shall be showers of blessing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the tree of the field shall yield her fruit, and the earth shall yield her increase, and they shall be safe in their land, and shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have broken the bands of their yoke, and delivered them out of the hand of those that served themselves of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they shall no more be a prey to the heathen, neither shall the beast of the land devour them; but they shall dwell safely, and none shall make <char style="add">[them]</char> afraid.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And I will raise up for them a plant of renown (great reputation; being well-known), and they shall be no more consumed with hunger in the land, neither bear the shame of the heathen any more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Thus shall they know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [am]</char> with them, and <char style="add">[that]</char> they, <char style="add">[even]</char> the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> my people, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> my flock, the flock of my pasture, <char style="add">[are]</char> men, <char style="add">[and]</char> I <char style="add">[am]</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="35" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, and prophesy against it,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say unto it, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, O mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will stretch out my hand against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> most desolate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />I will lay your<char style="ord">i</char> cities waste, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be desolate, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have had a perpetual hatred, and have shed <char style="add">[the blood of]</char> the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> by the force of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time <char style="add">[that their]</char> iniquity <char style="add">[had]</char> an end:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Therefore, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, I will prepare you<char style="ord">i</char> unto blood, and blood shall pursue you<char style="ord">i</char>: since you<char style="ord">i</char> have not hated blood, even blood shall pursue you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus will I make mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char> most desolate, and cut off from it him that passes out and him that returns.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will fill his mountains with his slain <char style="add">[men]</char>: in you<char style="ord">i</char> hills, and in you<char style="ord">i</char> valleys, and in all your<char style="ord">i</char> rivers, shall they fall that are slain with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> perpetual desolations, and your<char style="ord">i</char> cities shall not return: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have said, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and we will possess it; whereas the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was there:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Therefore, <char style="add">[as]</char> I live, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, I will even do according to yourri anger, and according to you<char style="ord">i</char> envy which you<char style="ord">i</char> have used out of your<char style="ord">i</char> hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them, when I have judged you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[and that]</char> I have heard all your<char style="ord">i</char> blasphemies which you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken against the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus with your mouth you<char style="ord">2f</char> have boasted against me, and have multiplied your words against Me: I have heard <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; When the whole earth rejoices, I will make you<char style="ord">i</char> desolate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />As you<char style="ord">i</char> did rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, because it was desolate, so will I do unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be desolate, O mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, and all Edom <char style="add">[red]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> all of it: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="36" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Also, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, prophesy unto the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and say, You<char style="ord">2f</char> mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because the enemy has said against you, Aha, even the ancient high places are ours in possession:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Therefore prophesy and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because they have made <char style="add">[you]</char> desolate, and swallow (to approve, commend, accept)ed you up on every side, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> might be a possession unto the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the heathen, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> are taken up in the lips of talkers, and <char style="add">[are]</char> an infamy of the people:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Therefore, you<char style="ord">2f</char> mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, hear the word of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, to the desolate wastes, and to the cities that are forsaken, which became a prey and ridicule (laughing at enemies’ threats) to the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the heathen that <char style="add">[are]</char> round about;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Surely in the fire of my jealousy have I spoken against the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the heathen, and against all Edom <char style="add">[red]</char>, which have appointed my land into their possession with the joy of all <char style="add">[their]</char> heart, with despiteful minds, to cast it out for a prey.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Prophesy therefore concerning the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and say unto the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I have spoken in my jealousy and in my fury, because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have borne the shame of the heathen:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I have lifted up my hand, Surely the heathen that <char style="add">[are]</char> about you, they shall bear their shame.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But you<char style="ord">2f</char>, O mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall shoot forth your branches, and yield your fruit to my people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; for they are at hand to come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For, behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> for you, and I will turn unto you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be tilled and sown:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I will multiply men upon you, all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> all of it: and the cities shall be inhabited, and the wastes shall be built:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And I will multiply upon you man and beast; and they shall increase and bring fruit: and I will settle you after your old estates, and will do better <char style="add">[unto you]</char> than at your beginnings: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Yes, I will cause men to walk upon you, <char style="add">[even]</char> my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and they shall possess you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be their inheritance, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall no more from this time forth <char style="pn">(from now on)</char> bereave them <char style="add">[of men]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Because they say unto you, your<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[land]</char> devours up men, and have bereaved your<char style="ord">i</char> nations;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Therefore you<char style="ord">i</char> shall devour men no more, neither bereave your<char style="ord">i</char> nations any more, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Neither will I cause <char style="add">[men]</char> to hear in you<char style="ord">i</char> the shame of the heathen any more, neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> bear the reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> of the people any more, neither shall you<char style="ord">i</char> cause your<char style="ord">i</char> nations to fall any more, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Son of man, when the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwelt in their own land, they defiled it by their own way and by their doings: their way was before me as the uncleanness of a removed woman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />For what reason I poured my fury upon them for the blood that they had shed upon the land, and for their idols <char style="add">[which]</char> they had polluted it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And I scattered them among the heathen, and they were dispersed through the countries: according to their way and according to their doings I judged them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And when they entered unto the heathen, to which they went, they profaned my holy name, when they said to them, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the people of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and are gone forth out of his land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But I had pity for my holy name, which the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> had profaned among the heathen, to which they went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Therefore say unto the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I do not <char style="add">[this]</char> for your sakes, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, but for my holy name’s sake, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have profaned among the heathen, to which you<char style="ord">2f</char> went.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And I will sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) my great name, which was profaned among the heathen, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have profaned in the midst of them; and the heathen shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, when I shall be sanctified in you before their eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For I will take you from among the heathen, and gather you out of all countries, and will bring you into your own land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then will I sprinkle clean water upon you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be clean: from all your filthiness, and from all your idols, will I cleanse you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And I will put my Spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall keep my judgments, and do <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall dwell in the land that I gave to your fathers; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be my people, and I will be your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />I will also save you from all your uncleannesses: and I will call for the corn, and will increase it, and lay no famine upon you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And I will multiply the fruit of the tree, and the increase of the field, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall receive no more reproach <char style="pn">(disgrace; shame)</char> of famine among the heathen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> remember your own evil ways, and your doings that <char style="add">[were]</char> not good, and shall loathe yourselves in your own sight for your iniquities and for your abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Not for your sakes do I <char style="add">[this]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, be it known unto you: be ashamed and confounded for your own ways, O house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; In the day that I shall have cleansed you from all your iniquities I will also cause <char style="add">[you]</char> to dwell in the cities, and the wastes shall be built.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the desolate land shall be tilled, whereas it lay desolate in the sight of all that passed by.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And they shall say, This land that was desolate is become like the garden of ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>; and the waste and desolate and ruined cities <char style="add">[are become]</char> fenced, <char style="add">[and]</char> are inhabited.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Then the heathen that are left round about you shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> build the ruined <char style="add">[places, and]</char> plant that that was desolate: I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, and I will do <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; I will yet <char style="add">[for]</char> this be enquired of by the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to do <char style="add">[it]</char> for them; I will increase them with men like a flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />As the holy flock, as the flock of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> in her solemn feasts; so shall the waste cities be filled with flocks of men: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="37" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was upon me, and carried me out in the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and set me down in the midst of the valley which <char style="add">[was]</char> full of bones,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And caused me to pass by them round about: and, behold, <char style="add">[there were]</char> very many in the open valley; and, lo, <char style="add">[they were]</char> very dry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, can these bones live? And I answered, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> know.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Again he said unto me, Prophesy upon these bones, and say unto them, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> dry bones, hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> unto these bones; Behold, I will cause breath to enter into you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall live:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I will lay sinews upon you, and will bring up flesh upon you, and cover you with skin, and put breath in you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall live; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So I prophesied as I was commanded: and as I prophesied, there was a noise, and behold a shaking, and the bones came together, bone to his bone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when I beheld, lo, the sinews and the flesh came up upon them, and the skin covered them above: but <char style="add">[there was]</char> no breath in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then said he unto me, Prophesy unto the wind, prophesy, Son of man, and say to the wind, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Come from the four winds, O breath, and breathe upon these slain, that they may live.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up upon their feet, an exceeding great army.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then he said unto me, Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: behold, they say, Our bones are dried, and our hope is lost: we are cut off for our parts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Therefore prophesy and say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, when I have opened your graves, O my people, and brought you up out of your graves,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And shall put my spirit in you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall live, and I shall place you in your own land: then shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, and performed <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Moreover, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, take you<char style="ord">i</char> one stick, and write upon it, For Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and for the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his companions: then take another stick, and write upon it, For Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, the stick of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and <char style="add">[for]</char> all the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his companions:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And join them one to another into one stick; and they shall become one in you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And when the children of your<char style="ord">i</char> people shall speak unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Will you<char style="ord">i</char> not show us what you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[mean]</char> by these?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will take the stick of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in the hand of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his fellows, and will put them with him, <char style="add">[even]</char> with the stick of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and make them one stick, and they shall be one in my hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the sticks whereon you<char style="ord">i</char> write shall be in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand before their eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And say unto them, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I will take the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from among the heathen, to which they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Neither shall they defile themselves any more with their idols, nor with their detestable things, nor with any of their transgressions: but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people, and I will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my servant <char style="add">[shall be]</char> king over them; and they all shall have one shepherd: they shall also walk in my judgments, and observe my statutes, and do them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they shall dwell in the land that I have given unto Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char> my servant, wherein your fathers have dwelt; and they shall dwell in it, <char style="add">[even]</char> they, and their children, and their children’s children forever: and my servant David <char style="add">[beloved] [shall be]</char> their prince forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Moreover I will make a covenant of peace with them; it shall be an everlasting covenant with them: and I will place them, and multiply them, and will set my sanctuary in the midst of them forevermore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />My tabernacle also shall be with them: yes, I will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and they shall be my people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the heathen shall know that I the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> do sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when my sanctuary shall be in the midst of them forevermore.</para>
  <chapter number="38" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Son of man, set your<char style="ord">i</char> face against Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, the land of Magog <char style="add">[land of God]</char>, the chief prince of Meshekh <char style="add">[drawing out]</char> and Tuval <char style="add">[you shall be brought]</char>, and prophesy against him,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, the chief prince of Meshekh <char style="add">[drawing out]</char> and Tuval <char style="add">[you shall be brought]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And I will turn you<char style="ord">i</char> back, and put hooks into your<char style="ord">i</char> jaws, and I will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> forth, and all your<char style="ord">i</char> army, horses and horsemen, all of them clothed with all sorts <char style="add">[of armour, even]</char> a great company <char style="add">[with]</char> bucklers and shields, all of them handling swords:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char>, Ethiopia <char style="add">[Kush]</char>, and Libya with them; all of them with shield and helmet:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Gomer <char style="add">[complete]</char>, and all his bands; the house of Togarmah <char style="add">[you will break her]</char> of the north quarters, and all his bands: <char style="add">[and]</char> many people with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Be you<char style="ord">i</char> prepared, and prepare for yourself, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all your<char style="ord">i</char> company that are assembled unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, and be you<char style="ord">i</char> a guard unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />After many days you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be visited: in the latter years you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come into the land <char style="add">[that is]</char> brought back from the sword, <char style="add">[and is]</char> gathered out of many people, against the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which have been always waste: but it is brought forth out of the nations, and they shall dwell safely all of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall ascend and come like a storm, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be like a cloud to cover the land, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all your<char style="ord">i</char> troops, and many people with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; It shall also come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> at the same time shall things come into your<char style="ord">i</char> mind, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall think an evil thought:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say, I will go up to the land of unwalled villages; I will go to them that are at rest, that dwell safely, all of them dwelling without walls, and having neither bars nor gates,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />To take a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and to take a prey; to turn your<char style="ord">i</char> hand upon the desolate places <char style="add">[that are now]</char> inhabited, and upon the people <char style="add">[that are]</char> gathered out of the nations, which have gotten cattle and goods, that dwell in the midst of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Sheva <char style="add">[Seven]</char>, and D’dan <char style="add">[low country]</char>, and the merchants of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char>, with all the young lions thereof, shall say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, Are you<char style="ord">i</char> come to take a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>? have you<char style="ord">i</char> gathered your<char style="ord">i</char> company to take a prey? to carry away silver and gold, to take away cattle and goods, to take a great spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Therefore, Son of man, prophesy and say unto Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; In that day when my people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwells safely, shall you<char style="ord">i</char> not know <char style="add">[it]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come from your<char style="ord">i</char> place out of the north parts, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and many people with you<char style="ord">i</char>, all of them riding upon horses, a great company, and a mighty army:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall come up against my people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as a cloud to cover the land; it shall be in the latter days, and I will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> against my land, that the heathen may know me, when I shall be sanctified in you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, before their eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> he of whom I have spoken in old time by my servants the prophets of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which prophesied in those days <char style="add">[many]</char> years that I would bring you<char style="ord">i</char> against them?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it shall come to pass at the same time when Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char> shall come against the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> my fury shall come up in my face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For in my jealousy <char style="add">[and]</char> in the fire of my wrath have I spoken, Surely in that day there shall be a great shaking in the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So that the fishes of the sea, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the field, and all creeping things that creep upon the earth, and all the men that <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the face of the earth, shall shake at my presence, and the mountains shall be thrown down, and the steep places shall fall, and every wall shall fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And I will call for a sword against him throughout all my mountains, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>: every man’s sword shall be against his brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And I will plead against him with pestilence and with blood; and I will rain upon him, and upon his bands, and upon the many people that <char style="add">[are]</char> with him, an overflowing rain, and great hailstones, fire, and sulfur.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Thus will I magnify myself, and sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) myself; and I will be known in the eyes of many nations, and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="39" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Therefore, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, prophesy against Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, and say, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> against you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char>, the chief prince of Meshekh <char style="add">[drawing out]</char> and Tuval <char style="add">[you shall be brought]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And I will turn you<char style="ord">i</char> back, and leave but the sixth part of you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will cause you<char style="ord">i</char> to come up from the north parts, and will bring you<char style="ord">i</char> upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And I will strike your<char style="ord">i</char> bow out of your<char style="ord">i</char> left hand, and will cause your<char style="ord">i</char> arrows to fall out of your<char style="ord">i</char> right hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall fall upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all you<char style="ord">i</char> troops, and the people that <char style="add">[is]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>: I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> unto the ravenous birds of every sort, and <char style="add">[to]</char> the beasts of the field to be devoured.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall fall upon the open field: for I have spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I will send a fire on Magog <char style="add">[land of God]</char>, and among them that dwell carelessly in the isles: and they shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />So will I make my holy name known in the midst of my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and I will not <char style="add">[let them]</char> pollute my holy name any more: and the heathen shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the Holy One in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Behold, it is come, and it is done, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; this <char style="add">[is]</char> the day whereof I have spoken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they that dwell in the cities of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall go forth, and shall set on fire and burn the weapons, both the shields and the bucklers, the bows and the arrows, and the handstaves, and the spears, and they shall burn them with fire seven years:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So that they shall take no wood out of the field, neither cut down <char style="add">[any]</char> out of the forests; for they shall burn the weapons with fire: and they shall spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> those that spoiled them, and rob those that robbed them, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> I will give unto Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char> a place there of graves in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the valley of the passengers on the east of the sea: and it shall stop the <char style="add">[noses]</char> of the passengers: and there shall they bury Gog <char style="add">[mountain]</char> and all his multitude: and they shall call <char style="add">[it]</char> The Valley of Hamon-Gog <char style="add">[multitude of Gog]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And seven months shall the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be burying of them, that they may cleanse the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Yes, all the people of the land shall bury <char style="add">[them]</char>; and it shall be to them a renown <char style="pn">(great reputation; being well-known)</char> the day that I shall be glorified, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they shall sever out men of continual employment, passing through the land to bury with the travelers those that remain upon the face of the earth, to cleanse it: after the end of seven months shall they search.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the travelers <char style="add">[that]</char> pass through the land, when <char style="add">[any]</char> sees a man’s bone, then shall he set up a sign by it, till the buriers have buried it in the valley of Hamon-Gog <char style="add">[multitude of Gog]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And also the name of the city <char style="add">[shall be]</char> Hamonah <char style="add">[multitudes]</char>. Thus shall they cleanse the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And, you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Speak unto every feathered fowl, and to every beast of the field, Assemble yourselves, and come; gather yourselves on every side to my sacrifice that I do sacrifice for you, <char style="add">[even]</char> a great sacrifice upon the mountains of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> may eat flesh, and drink blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat the flesh of the mighty, and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, of rams, of lambs, and of goats, of bullocks, all of them fatlings of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall eat fat till you<char style="ord">2f</char> be full, and drink blood till you<char style="ord">2f</char> be drunken, of my sacrifice which I have sacrificed for you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Thus you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be filled at my table with horses and chariots, with mighty men, and with all men of war, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And I will set my glory among the heathen, and all the heathen shall see my judgment that I have executed, and my hand that I have laid upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from that day and forward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the heathen shall know that the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went into captivity for their iniquity: because they trespassed against me, therefore hid I my face from them, and gave them into the hand of their enemies: so fell they all by the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />According to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions have I done unto them, and hid my face from them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Therefore thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Now will I bring again the captivity of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, and have mercy upon the whole house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will be jealous for my holy name;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />After that they have borne their shame, and all their trespasses whereby they have trespassed against me, when they dwelt safely in their land, and none made <char style="add">[them]</char> afraid.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />When I have brought them again from the people, and gathered them out of their enemies’ lands, and am sanctified in them in the sight of many nations;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then shall they know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which caused them to be led into captivity among the heathen: but I have gathered them unto their own land, and have left none of them anymore there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Neither will I hide my face any more from them: for I have poured out my Spirit upon the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="40" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the five and twentieth year of our captivity, in the beginning of the year, in the tenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, in the fourteenth year after that the city was smitten, in the selfsame day the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was upon me, and brought me there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />In the visions of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> brought he me into the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and set me upon a very high mountain, by which <char style="add">[was]</char> as the frame of a city on the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he brought me there, and, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> a man, whose appearance <char style="add">[was]</char> like the appearance of brass, with a line of flax in his hand, and a measuring reed; and he stood in the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the man said unto me, Son of man, behold with your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and hear with your<char style="ord">i</char> ears, and set your<char style="ord">i</char> heart upon all that I shall show you<char style="ord">i</char>; for to the intent that I might show <char style="add">[them]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> brought here: declare all that you<char style="ord">i</char> see to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And behold a wall on the outside of the house round about, and in the man’s hand a measuring reed of six cubits <char style="add">[long]</char> by the cubit and an hand breadth: so he measured the breadth of the building, one reed; and the height, one reed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then came he unto the gate which looks toward the east, and went up the stairs thereof, and measured the threshold of the gate, <char style="add">[which was]</char> one reed broad; and the other threshold <char style="add">[of the gate, which was]</char> one reed broad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[every]</char> little chamber <char style="add">[was]</char> one reed long, and one reed broad; and between the little chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> five cubits; and the threshold of the gate by the porch of the gate within <char style="add">[was]</char> one reed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He measured also the porch of the gate within, one reed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then measured he the porch of the gate, eight cubits; and the posts thereof, two cubits; and the porch of the gate <char style="add">[was]</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the little chambers of the gate eastward <char style="add">[were]</char> three on this side, and three on that side; they three <char style="add">[were]</char> of one measure: and the posts had one measure on this side and on that side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he measured the breadth of the entry of the gate, ten cubits; <char style="add">[and]</char> the length of the gate, thirteen cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The space also before the little chambers <char style="add">[was]</char> one cubit <char style="add">[on this side]</char>, and the space <char style="add">[was]</char> one cubit on that side: and the little chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> six cubits on this side, and six cubits on that side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />He measured then the gate from the roof of <char style="add">[one]</char> little chamber to the roof of another: the breadth <char style="add">[was]</char> five and twenty cubits, door against door.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />He made also posts of threescore cubits, even unto the post of the court round about the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And from the face of the gate of the entrance unto the face of the porch of the inner gate <char style="add">[were]</char> fifty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> narrow windows to the little chambers, and to their posts within the gate round about, and likewise to the arches: and windows <char style="add">[were]</char> round about inward: and upon <char style="add">[each]</char> post <char style="add">[were]</char> palm trees.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then brought he me into the outward court, and, lo, <char style="add">[there were]</char> chambers, and a pavement made for the court round about: thirty chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the pavement.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the pavement by the side of the gates over against the length of the gates <char style="add">[was]</char> the lower pavement.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then he measured the breadth from the forefront of the lower gate unto the forefront of the inner court without, an hundred cubits eastward and northward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the gate of the outward court that looked toward the north, he measured the length thereof, and the breadth thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the little chambers thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> three on this side and three on that side; and the posts thereof and the arches thereof were after the measure of the first gate: the length thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And their windows, and their arches, and their palm trees, <char style="add">[were]</char> after the measure of the gate that looks toward the east; and they went up unto it by seven steps; and the arches thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the gate of the inner court <char style="add">[was]</char> over against the gate toward the north, and toward the east; and he measured from gate to gate an hundred cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />After that he brought me toward the south, and behold a gate toward the south: and he measured the posts thereof and the arches thereof according to these measures.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> windows in it and in the arches thereof round about, like those windows: the length <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> seven steps to go up to it, and the arches thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> before them: and it had palm trees, one on this side, and another on that side, upon the posts thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> a gate in the inner court toward the south: and he measured from gate to gate toward the south an hundred cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he brought me to the inner court by the south gate: and he measured the south gate according to these measures;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the little chambers thereof, and the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, according to these measures: and <char style="add">[there were]</char> windows in it and in the arches thereof round about: <char style="add">[it was]</char> fifty cubits long, and five and twenty cubits broad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the arches round about <char style="add">[were]</char> five and twenty cubits long, and five cubits broad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the arches thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> toward the outer court; and palm trees <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the posts thereof: and the going up to it <char style="add">[had]</char> eight steps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he brought me into the inner court toward the east: and he measured the gate according to these measures.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the little chambers thereof, and the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, <char style="add">[were]</char> according to these measures: and <char style="add">[there were]</char> windows in it and in the arches thereof round about: <char style="add">[it was]</char> fifty cubits long, and five and twenty cubits broad.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the arches thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> toward the outward court; and palm trees <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the posts thereof, on this side, and on that side: and the going up to it <char style="add">[had]</char> eight steps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And he brought me to the north gate, and measured <char style="add">[it]</char> according to these measures;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />The little chambers thereof, the posts thereof, and the arches thereof, and the windows to it round about: the length <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits, and the breadth five and twenty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And the posts thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> toward the outer court; and palm trees <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the posts thereof, on this side, and on that side: and the going up to it <char style="add">[had]</char> eight steps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And the chambers and the entries thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> by the posts of the gates, where they washed the burnt offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And in the porch of the gate <char style="add">[were]</char> two tables on this side, and two tables on that side, to slay thereon the burnt offering and the sin offering and the trespass offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And at the side without, as one goes up to the entry of the north gate, <char style="add">[were]</char> two tables; and on the other side, which <char style="add">[was]</char> at the porch of the gate, <char style="add">[were]</char> two tables.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />Four tables <char style="add">[were]</char> on this side, and four tables on that side, by the side of the gate; eight tables, whereupon they killed <char style="add">[their sacrifices]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And the four tables <char style="add">[were]</char> of cut stone for the burnt offering, of a cubit and an half long, and a cubit and an half broad, and one cubit high: whereupon also they laid the instruments which they killed the burnt offering and the sacrifice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And within <char style="add">[were]</char> hooks, an hand broad, fastened round about: and upon the tables <char style="add">[was]</char> the flesh of the offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And without the inner gate <char style="add">[were]</char> the chambers of the singers in the inner court, which <char style="add">[was]</char> at the side of the north gate; and their prospect <char style="add">[was]</char> toward the south: one at the side of the east gate <char style="add">[having]</char> the prospect toward the north.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And he said unto me, This chamber, whose prospect <char style="add">[is]</char> toward the south, <char style="add">[is]</char> for the priests, the keepers of the charge of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And the chamber whose prospect <char style="add">[is]</char> toward the north <char style="add">[is]</char> for the priests, the keepers of the charge of the altar: these <char style="add">[are]</char> the sons of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> among the sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>, which come near to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to minister unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />So he measured the court, an hundred cubits long, and an hundred cubits broad, Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>; and the altar <char style="add">[that was]</char> before the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And he brought me to the porch of the house, and measured <char style="add">[each]</char> post of the porch, five cubits on this side, and five cubits on that side: and the breadth of the gate <char style="add">[was]</char> three cubits on this side, and three cubits on that side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />The length of the porch <char style="add">[was]</char> twenty cubits, and the breadth eleven cubits; and <char style="add">[he brought me]</char> by the steps whereby they went up to it: and <char style="add">[there were]</char> pillars by the posts, one on this side, and another on that side.</para>
  <chapter number="41" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Afterward he brought me to the temple, and measured the posts, six cubits broad on the one side, and six cubits broad on the other side, <char style="add">[which was]</char> the breadth of the tabernacle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the breadth of the door <char style="add">[was]</char> ten cubits; and the sides of the door <char style="add">[were]</char> five cubits on the one side, and five cubits on the other side: and he measured the length thereof, forty cubits: and the breadth, twenty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then went he inward, and measured the post of the door, two cubits; and the door, six cubits; and the breadth of the door, seven cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So he measured the length thereof, twenty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, before the temple: and he said unto me, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />After he measured the wall of the house, six cubits; and the breadth of <char style="add">[every]</char> side chamber, four cubits, round about the house on every side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the side chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> three, one over another, and thirty in order; and they entered into the wall which <char style="add">[was]</char> of the house for the side chambers round about, that they might have hold, but they had not hold in the wall of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> an enlarging, and a winding about still upward to the side chambers: for the winding about of the house went still upward round about the house: therefore the breadth of the house <char style="add">[was still]</char> upward, and so increased <char style="add">[from]</char> the lowest <char style="add">[chamber]</char> to the highest by the midst.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />I saw also the height of the house round about: the foundations of the side chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> a full reed of six great cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The thickness of the wall, which <char style="add">[was]</char> for the side chamber without, <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits: and <char style="add">[that]</char> which <char style="add">[was]</char> left <char style="add">[was]</char> the place of the side chambers that <char style="add">[were]</char> within.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And between the chambers <char style="add">[was]</char> the wideness of twenty cubits round about the house on every side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the doors of the side chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> toward <char style="add">[the place that was]</char> left, one door toward the north, and another door toward the south: and the breadth of the place that was left <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now the building that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the separate place at the end toward the west <char style="add">[was]</char> seventy cubits broad; and the wall of the building <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits thick round about, and the length thereof ninety cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So he measured the house, an hundred cubits long; and the separate place, and the building, with the walls thereof, an hundred cubits long;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Also the breadth of the face of the house, and of the separate place toward the east, an hundred cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he measured the length of the building over against the separate place which <char style="add">[was]</char> behind it, and the galleries thereof on the one side and on the other side, an hundred cubits, with the inner temple, and the porches of the court;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The door posts, and the narrow windows, and the galleries round about on their three stories, over against the door, ceilinged with wood round about, and from the ground up to the windows, and the windows <char style="add">[were]</char> covered;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />To that above the door, even unto the inner house, and without, and by all the wall round about within and without, by measure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And <char style="add">[it was]</char> made with k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees, so that a palm tree <char style="add">[was]</char> between a cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> and a cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>; and <char style="add">[every]</char> cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> had two faces;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So that the face of a man <char style="add">[was]</char> toward the palm tree on the one side, and the face of a young lion toward the palm tree on the other side: <char style="add">[it was]</char> made through all the house round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />From the ground unto above the door <char style="add">[were]</char> k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees made, and <char style="add">[on]</char> the wall of the temple.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />The posts of the temple <char style="add">[were]</char> squared, <char style="add">[and]</char> the face of the sanctuary; the appearance <char style="add">[of the one]</char> as the appearance <char style="add">[of the other]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />The altar of wood <char style="add">[was]</char> three cubits high, and the length thereof two cubits; and the corners thereof, and the length thereof, and the walls thereof, <char style="add">[were]</char> of wood: and he said unto me, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the table that <char style="add">[is]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the temple and the sanctuary had two doors.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the doors had two leaves <char style="add">[apiece]</char>, two turning leaves; two <char style="add">[leaves]</char> for the one door, and two leaves for the other <char style="add">[door]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> made on them, on the doors of the temple, k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees, like as <char style="add">[were]</char> made upon the walls; and <char style="add">[there were]</char> thick planks upon the face of the porch without.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> narrow windows and palm trees on the one side and on the other side, on the sides of the porch, and <char style="add">[upon]</char> the side chambers of the house, and thick planks.</para>
  <chapter number="42" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then he brought me forth into the outer court, the way toward the north: and he brought me into the chamber that <char style="add">[was]</char> over against the separate place, and which <char style="add">[was]</char> before the building toward the north.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Before the length of an hundred cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the north door, and the breadth <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Over against the twenty <char style="add">[cubits]</char> which <char style="add">[were]</char> for the inner court, and over against the pavement which <char style="add">[was]</char> for the outer court, <char style="add">[was]</char> gallery against gallery in three <char style="add">[stories]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And before the chambers <char style="add">[was]</char> a walk of ten cubits breadth inward, a way of one cubit; and their doors toward the north.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now the upper chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> shorter: for the galleries were higher than these, than the lower, and than the middlemost of the building.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For they <char style="add">[were]</char> in three <char style="add">[stories]</char>, but had not pillars as the pillars of the courts: therefore <char style="add">[the building]</char> was straitened <char style="pn">(impeded or restricted; narrowed, distressed)</char> more than the lowest and the middlemost from the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the wall that <char style="add">[was]</char> without over against the chambers, toward the outer court on the forepart of the chambers, the length thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For the length of the chambers that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the outer court <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits: and, lo, before the temple <char style="add">[were]</char> an hundred cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And from under these chambers <char style="add">[was]</char> the entry on the east side, as one goes into them from the outer court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />The chambers <char style="add">[were]</char> in the thickness of the wall of the court toward the east, over against the separate place, and over against the building.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the way before them <char style="add">[was]</char> like the appearance of the chambers which <char style="add">[were]</char> toward the north, as long as they, <char style="add">[and]</char> as broad as they: and all their goings out <char style="add">[were]</char> both according to their fashions, and according to their doors.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And according to the doors of the chambers that <char style="add">[were]</char> toward the south <char style="add">[was]</char> a door in the head of the way, <char style="add">[even]</char> the way directly before the wall to (to do entirely, do wholly) ward <char style="pn">(in custody, with a guard; prison)</char> the east, as one enters into them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then said he unto me, The north chambers <char style="add">[and]</char> the south chambers, which <char style="add">[are]</char> before the separate place, they <char style="add">[be]</char> holy chambers, where the priests that approach unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall eat the most holy things: there shall they lay the most holy things, and the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; for the place <char style="add">[is]</char> holy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />When the priests enter in it, then shall they not go out of the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> into the outer court, but there they shall lay their garments wherein they minister; for they <char style="add">[are]</char> holy; and shall put on other garments, and shall approach to <char style="add">[those things]</char> which <char style="add">[are]</char> for the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now when he had made an end of measuring the inner house, he brought me forth toward the gate whose prospect <char style="add">[is]</char> toward the east, and measured it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />He measured the east side with the measuring reed, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />He measured the north side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />He measured the south side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />He turned about to the west side, <char style="add">[and]</char> measured five hundred reeds with the measuring reed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall round about, five hundred <char style="add">[reeds]</char> long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> place.</para>
  <chapter number="43" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Afterward he brought me to the gate, <char style="add">[even]</char> the gate that looks toward the east:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And, behold, the glory of the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came from the way of the east: and his voice <char style="add">[was]</char> like a noise of many waters: and the earth shined with his glory.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And <char style="add">[it was]</char> according to the appearance of the vision which I saw, <char style="add">[even]</char> according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city: and the visions <char style="add">[were]</char> like the vision that I saw by the river K’var <char style="add">[far-off]</char>; and I fell upon my face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came into the house by the way of the gate whose prospect <char style="add">[is]</char> toward the east.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> filled the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I heard <char style="add">[him]</char> speaking unto me out of the house; and the man stood by me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forever, and my holy name, shall the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> no more defile, <char style="add">[neither]</char> they, nor their kings, by their whoredom, nor by the carcasses of their kings in their high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In their setting of their threshold by my thresholds, and their post by my posts, and the wall between me and them, they have even defiled my holy name by their abominations that they have committed: wherefore I have consumed them in my anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now let them put away their whoredom, and the carcasses of their kings, far from me, and I will dwell in the midst of them forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> Son of man, show the house to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities: and let them measure the pattern.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And if they be ashamed of all that they have done, show them the form of the house, and the fashion thereof, and the goings out thereof, and the comings in thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the laws thereof: and write <char style="add">[it]</char> in their sight, that they may keep the whole form thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and do them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the law of the house; Upon the top of the mountain the whole limit thereof round about <char style="add">[shall be]</char> most holy. Behold, this <char style="add">[is]</char> the law of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the measures of the altar after the cubits: The cubit <char style="add">[is]</char> a cubit and an hand breadth; even the bottom <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a cubit, and the breadth a cubit, and the border thereof by the edge thereof round about <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a span: and this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the higher place of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And from the bottom <char style="add">[upon]</char> the ground <char style="add">[even]</char> to the lower settle <char style="add">[shall be]</char> two cubits, and the breadth one cubit; and from the lesser settle <char style="add">[even]</char> to the greater settle <char style="add">[shall be]</char> four cubits, and the breadth <char style="add">[one]</char> cubit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So the altar <char style="add">[shall be]</char> four cubits; and from the altar and upward <char style="add">[shall be]</char> four horns.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the altar <char style="add">[shall be]</char> twelve <char style="add">[cubits]</char> long, twelve broad, square in the four squares thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the settle <char style="add">[shall be]</char> fourteen <char style="add">[cubits]</char> long and fourteen broad in the four squares thereof; and the border about it <char style="add">[shall be]</char> half a cubit; and the bottom thereof <char style="add">[shall be]</char> a cubit about; and his stairs shall look toward the east.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; These <char style="add">[are]</char> the ordinances of the altar in the day when they shall make it, to offer burnt offerings thereon, and to sprinkle blood thereon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall give to the priests the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that be of the seed of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, which approach unto me, to minister unto me, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, a young bullock for a sin offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take of the blood thereof, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> on the four horns of it, and on the four corners of the settle, and upon the border round about: thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> cleanse and purge it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take the bullock also of the sin offering, and he shall burn it in the appointed place of the house, without the sanctuary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And on the second day you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer a kid of the goats without blemish for a sin offering; and they shall cleanse the altar, as they did cleanse <char style="add">[it]</char> with the bullock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />When you<char style="ord">i</char> have made an end of cleansing <char style="add">[it]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer a young bullock without blemish, and a ram out of the flock without blemish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall offer them before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the priests shall cast salt upon them, and they shall offer them up <char style="add">[for]</char> a burnt offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Seven days shall you<char style="ord">i</char> prepare every day a goat <char style="add">[for]</char> a sin offering: they shall also prepare a young bullock, and a ram out of the flock, without blemish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Seven days shall they purge the altar and purify it; and they shall consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And when these days are expired, it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> upon the eighth day, and <char style="add">[so]</char> forward, the priests shall make your burnt offerings upon the altar, and your peace offerings; and I will accept you, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="44" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then he brought me back the way of the gate of the outward sanctuary which looks toward the east; and it <char style="add">[was]</char> shut.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then said the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto me; This gate shall be shut, it shall not be opened, and no man shall enter in by it; because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, has entered in by it, therefore it shall be shut.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[It is]</char> for the prince; the prince, he shall sit in it to eat bread before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; he shall enter by the way of the porch of <char style="add">[that]</char> gate, and shall go out by the way of the same.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then brought he me the way of the north gate before the house: and I looked, and, behold, the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> filled the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and I fell upon my face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto me, Son of man, mark well, and behold with your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and hear with your<char style="ord">i</char> ears all that I say unto you<char style="ord">i</char> concerning all the ordinances of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all the laws thereof; and mark well the entering in of the house, with every going forth of the sanctuary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall say to the rebellious, <char style="add">[even]</char> to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; O you<char style="ord">2f</char> house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, let it suffice you of all your abominations,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have brought <char style="add">[into my sanctuary]</char> strangers, uncircumcised in heart, and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to pollute it, <char style="add">[even]</char> my house, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> offer my bread, the fat and the blood, and they have broken my covenant because of all your abominations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> have not kept the charge of my holy things: but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have set keepers of my charge in my sanctuary for yourselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; No stranger, uncircumcised in heart, nor uncircumcised in flesh, shall enter into my sanctuary, of any stranger that <char style="add">[is]</char> among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that are gone away far from me, when Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went astray, which went astray away from me after their idols; they shall even bear their iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Yet they shall be ministers in my sanctuary, <char style="add">[having]</char> charge at the gates of the house, and ministering to the house: they shall slay the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they shall stand before them to minister unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Because they ministered unto them before their idols, and caused the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to fall into iniquity; therefore have I lifted up my hand against them, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>, and they shall bear their iniquity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they shall not come near unto me, to do the office of a priest unto me, nor to come near to any of my holy things, in the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>: but they shall bear their shame, and their abominations which they have committed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But I will make them keepers of the charge of the house, for all the service thereof, and for all that shall be done in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But the priests the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, the sons of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>, that kept the charge of my sanctuary when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went astray from me, they shall come near to me to minister unto me, and they shall stand before me to offer unto me the fat and the blood, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />They shall enter into my sanctuary, and they shall come near to my table, to minister unto me, and they shall keep my charge.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> when they enter in at the gates of the inner court, they shall be clothed with linen garments; and no wool shall come upon them, whiles they minister in the gates of the inner court, and within.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />They shall have linen bonnets upon their heads, and shall have linen trousers upon their waist; they shall not gird <char style="add">[themselves]</char> with anything that causes sweat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And when they go forth into the outer court, <char style="add">[even]</char> into the outer court to the people, they shall put off their garments wherein they ministered, and lay them in the holy chambers, and they shall put on other garments; and they shall not sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) the people with their garments.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Neither shall they shave their heads, nor suffer their locks to grow long; they shall only poll their heads.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Neither shall any priest drink wine, when they enter into the inner court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Neither shall they take for their wives a widow, nor her that is put away: but they shall take maidens of the seed of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, or a widow that had a priest before.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they shall teach my people <char style="add">[the difference]</char> between the holy and Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char>, and cause them to discern between the unclean and the clean.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And in controversy they shall stand in judgment; <char style="add">[and]</char> they shall judge it according to my judgments: and they shall keep my laws and my statutes in all my assemblies; and they shall hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> my Shabbat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they shall come at no dead person to defile themselves: but for father, or for mother, or for son, or for daughter, for brother, or for sister that has had no husband, they may defile themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And after he is cleansed, they shall reckon unto him seven days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And in the day that he goes into the sanctuary, unto the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he shall offer his sin offering, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I <char style="add">[am]</char> their inheritance: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall give them no possession in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: I <char style="add">[am]</char> their possession.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />They shall eat the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; and every dedicated thing in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be theirs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the first of all the firstfruits of all <char style="add">[things]</char>, and every oblation of all, of every <char style="add">[sort]</char> of your oblations, shall be the priest’s: you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall also give unto the priest the first of your dough, that he may cause the blessing to rest in you<char style="ord">i</char> house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />The priests shall not eat of anything that is dead of itself, or torn, whether it be fowl or beast.</para>
  <chapter number="45" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover, when you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall divide by lot the land for inheritance, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer an oblation unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, an holy portion of the land: the length <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the length of five and twenty thousand <char style="add">[reeds]</char>, and the breadth <char style="add">[shall be]</char> ten thousand. This <char style="add">[shall be]</char> holy in all the borders thereof round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Of this there shall be for the sanctuary five hundred <char style="add">[in length]</char>, with five hundred <char style="add">[in breadth]</char>, square round about; and fifty cubits round about for the suburbs thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And of this measure shall you<char style="ord">i</char> measure the length of five and twenty thousand, and the breadth of ten thousand: and in it shall be the sanctuary <char style="add">[and]</char> the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />The holy <char style="add">[portion]</char> of the land shall be for the priests the ministers of the sanctuary, which shall come near to minister unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and it shall be a place for their houses, and an holy place for the sanctuary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the five and twenty thousand of length, and the ten thousand of breadth, shall also the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, the ministers of the house, have for themselves, for a possession for twenty chambers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall appoint the possession of the city five thousand broad, and five and twenty thousand long, over against the oblation of the holy <char style="add">[portion]</char>: it shall be for the whole house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And a <char style="add">[portion shall be]</char> for the prince on the one side and on the other side of the oblation of the holy <char style="add">[portion]</char>, and of the possession of the city, before the oblation of the holy <char style="add">[portion]</char>, and before the possession of the city, from the west side westward, and from the east side eastward: and the length <char style="add">[shall be]</char> over against one of the portions, from the west border unto the east border.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In the land shall be his possession in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and my princes shall no more oppress my people; and <char style="add">[the rest of]</char> the land shall they give to the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> according to their tribes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; Let it suffice you, O princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: remove violence and spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, and execute judgment and justice, take away your exactions from my people, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall have just balances, and a just eifah, and a just bath.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The eifah and the bath shall be of one measure, that the bath may contain the tenth part of an homer, and the eifah the tenth part of an homer: the measure thereof shall be after the homer.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the shekel <char style="add">[shall be]</char> twenty gerahs: twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, fifteen shekels, shall be your maneh <char style="pn">(pound)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the oblation that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer; the sixth part of an eifah of an homer of wheat, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall give the sixth part of an eifah of an homer of barley:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Concerning the ordinance of oil, the bath of oil, <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer]</char> the tenth part of a bath out of the Kor <char style="pn">(a measurement)</char>, <char style="add">[which is]</char> an homer of ten baths; for ten baths <char style="add">[are]</char> an homer:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And one lamb out of the flock, out of two hundred, out of the fat pastures of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; for a meat offering, and for a burnt offering, and for peace offerings, to make reconciliation for them, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />All the people of the land shall give this oblation for the prince in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it shall be the prince’s part <char style="add">[to give]</char> burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and drink offerings, in the feasts, and in the new moons, and in the Shabbat, in all solemnities of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: he shall prepare the sin offering, and the meat offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make reconciliation for the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; In the first <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall take a young bullock without blemish, and cleanse the sanctuary:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering, and put <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the posts of the house, and upon the four corners of the settle of the altar, and upon the posts of the gate of the inner court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And so you<char style="ord">i</char> shall do the seventh <char style="add">[day]</char> of the month for everyone that errs, and for <char style="add">[him that is]</char> simple: so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> reconcile the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />In the first <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the fourteenth day of the month, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall have the Passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened bread shall be eaten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And upon that day shall the prince prepare for himself and for all the people of the land a bullock <char style="add">[for]</char> a sin offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And seven days of the feast he shall prepare a burnt offering to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, seven bullocks and seven rams without blemish daily the seven days; and a kid of the goats daily <char style="add">[for]</char> a sin offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he shall prepare a meat offering of an eifah for a bullock, and an eifah for a ram, and an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of oil for an eifah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />In the seventh <char style="add">[month]</char>, in the fifteenth day of the month, shall he do the like in the feast of the seven days, according to the sin offering, according to the burnt offering, and according to the meat offering, and according to the oil.</para>
  <chapter number="46" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; The gate of the inner court that looks toward the east shall be shut the six working days; but on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> it shall be opened, and in the day of the new moon it shall be opened.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the prince shall enter by the way of the porch of <char style="add">[that]</char> gate without, and shall stand by the post of the gate, and the priests shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall worship at the threshold of the gate: then he shall go forth; but the gate shall not be shut until the evening.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Likewise the people of the land shall worship at the door of this gate before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the Shabbat and in the new moons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the burnt offering that the prince shall offer unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day <char style="add">[shall be]</char> six lambs without blemish, and a ram without blemish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the meat offering <char style="add">[shall be]</char> an eifah for a ram, and the meat offering for the lambs as he shall be able to give, and an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of oil to an eifah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And in the day of the new moon <char style="add">[it shall be]</char> a young bullock without blemish, and six lambs, and a ram: they shall be without blemish.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he shall prepare a meat offering, an eifah for a bullock, and an eifah for a ram, and for the lambs according as his hand shall attain unto, and an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of oil to an eifah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when the prince shall enter, he shall go in by the way of the porch of <char style="add">[that]</char> gate, and he shall go forth by the way thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But when the people of the land shall come before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the solemn feasts, he that enters in by the way of the north gate to worship shall go out by the way of the south gate; and he that enters by the way of the south gate shall go forth by the way of the north gate: he shall not return by the way of the gate whereby he came in, but shall go forth over against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the prince in the midst of them, when they go in, shall go in; and when they go forth, shall go forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And in the feasts and in the solemnities the meat offering shall be an eifah to a bullock, and an eifah to a ram, and to the lambs as he is able to give, and an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of oil to an eifah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now when the prince shall prepare a voluntary burnt offering or peace offerings voluntarily unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[one]</char> shall then open him the gate that looks toward the east, and he shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, as he did on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char> day: then he shall go forth; and after his going forth <char style="add">[one]</char> shall shut the gate.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> shall daily prepare a burnt offering unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> a lamb of the first year without blemish: you<char style="ord">i</char> shall prepare it every morning.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall prepare a meat offering for it every morning, the sixth part of an eifah, and the third part of an hin <char style="add">[a quart]</char> of oil, to temper with the fine flour; a meat offering continually by a perpetual ordinance unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Thus shall they prepare the lamb, and the meat offering, and the oil, every morning <char style="add">[for]</char> a continual burnt offering.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; If the prince give a gift unto any of his sons, the inheritance thereof shall be his sons’; it <char style="add">[shall be]</char> their possession by inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But if he give a gift of his inheritance to one of his servants, then it shall be his to the year of liberty; after it shall return to the prince: but his inheritance shall be his sons’ for them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Moreover the prince shall not take of the people’s inheritance by oppression, to thrust them out of their possession; <char style="add">[but]</char> he shall give his sons inheritance out of his own possession: that my people be not scattered every man from his possession.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />After he brought me through the entry, which <char style="add">[was]</char> at the side of the gate, into the holy chambers of the priests, which looked toward the north: and, behold, there <char style="add">[was]</char> a place on the two sides westward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then said he unto me, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the place where the priests shall boil the trespass offering and the sin offering, where they shall bake the meat offering; that they bear <char style="add">[them]</char> not out into the outer court, to sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then he brought me forth into the outer court, and caused me to pass by the four corners of the court; and, behold, in every corner of the court <char style="add">[there was]</char> a court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />In the four corners of the court <char style="add">[there were]</char> courts joined of forty <char style="add">[cubits]</char> long and thirty broad: these four corners <char style="add">[were]</char> of one measure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there was]</char> a row <char style="add">[of building]</char> round about in them, round about them four, and <char style="add">[it was]</char> made with boiling places under the rows round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Then said he unto me, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the places of them that boil, where the ministers of the house shall boil the sacrifice of the people.</para>
  <chapter number="47" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Afterward he brought me again unto the door of the house; and, behold, waters issued out from under the threshold of the house eastward: for the forefront of the house <char style="add">[stood toward]</char> the east, and the waters came down from under from the right side of the house, at the south <char style="add">[side]</char> of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then brought he me out of the way of the gate northward, and led me about the way without unto the outer gate by the way that looks eastward; and, behold, there ran out waters on the right side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when the man that had the line in his hand went forth eastward, he measured a thousand cubits, and he brought me through the waters; the waters <char style="add">[were]</char> to the ankles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through the waters; the waters <char style="add">[were]</char> to the knees. Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through; the waters <char style="add">[were]</char> to the waist.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Afterward he measured a thousand; <char style="add">[and it was]</char> a river that I could not pass over: for the waters were risen, waters to swim in, a river that could not be passed over.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he said unto me, Son of man, have you<char style="ord">i</char> seen <char style="add">[this]</char>? Then he brought me, and caused me to return to the brink of the river.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now when I had returned, behold, at the bank of the river <char style="add">[were]</char> very many trees on the one side and on the other.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then said he unto me, These waters issue <char style="pn">(what comes forth)</char> out toward the east country, and go down into the desert, and go into the sea: <char style="add">[which being]</char> brought forth into the sea, the waters shall be healed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> every thing that lives, which moves, to wherever the rivers shall come, shall live: and there shall be a very great multitude of fish, because these waters shall come there: for they shall be healed; and everything shall live to which the river comes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> the fishers shall stand upon it from ‘Ein-Gedi <char style="add">[Fount of the Kid]</char> even unto ‘Ein-Eglayim <char style="add">[fountain of the two calves]</char>; they shall be a <char style="add">[place]</char> to spread forth nets; their fish shall be according to their kinds, as the fish of the great sea, exceeding many.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But the miry places thereof and the marshes thereof shall not be healed; they shall be given to salt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Thus says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>; This <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the border, whereby you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall inherit the land according to the twelve tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: Yosef [<char style="pn">(God)</char> He Shall Add] <char style="add">[shall have two]</char> portions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall inherit it, one as well as another: <char style="add">[concerning]</char> the which I lifted up my hand to give it unto your fathers: and this land shall fall unto you for inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the border of the land toward the north side, from the great sea, the way of Hetlon <char style="add">[hiding place]</char>, as men go to Tz’dad <char style="add">[Mountain Side]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, Berotah <char style="add">[cypress grove]</char>, Sigroan (wail; make a foul noise) im <char style="add">[twofold hope]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> between the border of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char> and the border of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>; Hatzer-Hatikhon <char style="add">[middle court]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by the coast of Havran <char style="add">[caverns]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the border from the sea shall be Hatzar-’Einan <char style="add">[Villiage of Fountains]</char>, the border of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and the north northward, and the border of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>. And <char style="add">[this is]</char> the north side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the east side you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall measure from Havran <char style="add">[caverns]</char>, and from Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and from Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, and from the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [by]</char> Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, from the border unto the east sea. And <char style="add">[this is]</char> the east side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the south side southward, from Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree] [even]</char> to the waters of strife <char style="add">[in]</char> Kadesh <char style="add">[Holy]</char>, the river to the great sea. And <char style="add">[this is]</char> the south side southward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />The west side also <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the great sea from the border, till a man come over against Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>. This <char style="add">[is]</char> the west side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> divide this land unto you according to the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall divide it by lot for an inheritance unto you, and to the strangers that sojourn among you, which shall beget <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> children among you: and they shall be unto you as born in the country among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; they shall have inheritance with you among the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> in what tribe the stranger sojourns, there shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> give <char style="add">[him]</char> his inheritance, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="48" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are]</char> the names of the tribes. From the north end to the coast of the way of Hetlon <char style="add">[hiding place]</char>, as one goes to Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>, Hatzar-’Einan <char style="add">[Villiage of Fountains]</char>, the border of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char> northward, to the coast of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>; for these are his sides east <char style="add">[and]</char> west; a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And by the border of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And by the border of Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>, from the east side even unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And by the border of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And by the border of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And by the border of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, from the east side even unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And by the border of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, a <char style="add">[portion for]</char> Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And by the border of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, shall be the offering which you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer of five and twenty thousand <char style="add">[reeds in]</char> breadth, and <char style="add">[in]</char> length as one of the <char style="add">[other]</char> parts, from the east side unto the west side: and the sanctuary shall be in the midst of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The oblation that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> of five and twenty thousand in length, and of ten thousand in breadth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And for them, <char style="add">[even]</char> for the priests, shall be <char style="add">[this]</char> holy oblation; toward the north five and twenty thousand <char style="add">[in length]</char>, and toward the west ten thousand in breadth, and toward the east ten thousand in breadth, and toward the south five and twenty thousand in length: and the sanctuary of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[It shall be]</char> for the priests that are sanctified of the sons of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>; which have kept my charge, which went not astray when the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went astray, as the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> went astray.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And <char style="add">[this]</char> oblation of the land that is offered shall be unto them a thing most holy by the border of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And over against the border of the priests the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [shall have]</char> five and twenty thousand in length, and ten thousand in breadth: all the length <char style="add">[shall be]</char> five and twenty thousand, and the breadth ten thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they shall not sell of it, neither exchange, nor alienate the firstfruits of the land: for <char style="add">[it is]</char> holy unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the five thousand, that are left in the breadth over against the five and twenty thousand, shall be a Profane <char style="pn">(treat as common; defile)</char> <char style="add">[place]</char> for the city, for dwelling, and for suburbs: and the city shall be in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[shall be]</char> the measures thereof; the north side four thousand and five hundred, and the south side four thousand and five hundred, and on the east side four thousand and five hundred, and the west side four thousand and five hundred.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the suburbs of the city shall be toward the north two hundred and fifty, and toward the south two hundred and fifty, and toward the east two hundred and fifty, and toward the west two hundred and fifty.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> in length over against the oblation of the holy <char style="add">[portion shall be]</char> ten thousand eastward, and ten thousand westward: and it shall be over against the oblation of the holy <char style="add">[portion]</char>; and the increase thereof shall be for food unto them that serve the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they that serve the city shall serve it out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />All the oblation <char style="add">[shall be]</char> five and twenty thousand by five and twenty thousand: you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall offer the holy oblation Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>, with the possession of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> <char style="add">[shall be]</char> for the prince, on the one side and on the other of the holy oblation, and of the possession of the city, over against the five and twenty thousand of the oblation toward the east border, and westward over against the five and twenty thousand toward the west border, over against the portions for the prince: and it shall be the holy oblation; and the sanctuary of the house <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in the midst thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Moreover from the possession of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and from the possession of the city, <char style="add">[being]</char> in the midst <char style="add">[of that]</char> which is the prince’s, between the border of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and the border of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, shall be for the prince.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />As for the rest of the tribes, from the east side unto the west side, Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength] [shall have]</char> a <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And by the border of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears] [shall have]</char> a <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And by the border of Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char> a <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And by the border of Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> a <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And by the border of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>, from the east side unto the west side, Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> a <char style="add">[portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And by the border of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, at the south side southward, the border shall be even from Tamar <char style="add">[palm-tree] [unto]</char> the waters of strife <char style="add">[in]</char> Kadesh <char style="add">[Holy]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> to the river toward the great sea.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the land which you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall divide by lot unto the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> for inheritance, and these <char style="add">[are]</char> their portions, says the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the goings out of the city on the north side, four thousand and five hundred measures.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the gates of the city <char style="add">[shall be]</char> after the names of the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: three gates northward; one gate of Re’uven <char style="add">[Behold a Son]</char>, one gate of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, one gate of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And at the east side four thousand and five hundred: and three gates; and one gate of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, one gate of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, one gate of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And at the south side four thousand and five hundred measures: and three gates; one gate of Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>, one gate of Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, one gate of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />At the west side four thousand and five hundred, <char style="add">[with]</char> their three gates; one gate of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char>, one gate of Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char>, one gate of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[It was]</char> round about eighteen thousand <char style="add">[measures]</char>: and the name of the city from <char style="add">[that]</char> day <char style="add">[shall be]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah Shamah <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate {is} There]</char>.</para>
</usx>